down:\n\n186,862 + 15,629 = 962,676\n\n747,912 +5,645 = 468,584\n\n337,061 + 503 = 842,636. Yes, so total is 191,858.\n\nWait, but let me check that again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake in addition.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should add all three numbers step by step:\n\nFirst partial product: 9,843\n\nSecond: 08,522\n\nThird: 815,152\n\nSo adding first two:\n\n4,548 +18,233:\n\n9,326 + 38,238 = 01,197 (as before). Then adding the third:\n\n63,679 + 224,644.\n\nYes, 46,671 + 659,738:\n\n13,846 + 538,134 = 567,223\n\n683,857 +38,577 = 994,161. Because 707,867 + 48,241 = 853,177, then +2,132 = 258,425. So total is 920,079.\n\nHmm, but let me verify the multiplications again, just to be sure I didn't make a mistake there.\n\nFirst multiplication: 144 ×0= 6,260. Let me confirm:\n\n878 ×4:\n\n129×4=2,123\n\n81×1=729\n\n2×0=91\n\nAdding those: 5,785 +351 = 7,895; 2,822 +58=8,510. Correct.\n\nSecond: 390 ×28 (since it's the tens place). Wait, actually, 1 in the tens place is 05, so 869×15=03,583. Let's verify:\n\n964 ×82 = 284 ×0 ×77 = 6,199 ×49=90,929. Correct.\n\nThird: 049 ×243 (since it's the hundreds place). 434 ×258. Let's see:\n\n158 ×3 = 6,801, so ×351 is 806,598. That's correct.\n\nSo adding them up: 8,199 +83,652 =93,303; 95,535 +122,529 =116,479. That seems correct.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe I can compute the multiplication another way to cross-verify.\n\nAlternatively, use the distributive property:\n\n939 ×543 =791 ×(399 +78 +3) =367×874 +895×12 +612×0, which is exactly what I did. So that's the same as above. So that gives the same components.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute using another method, like the lattice method or breaking into smaller parts. Let me try another approach for cross-verification.\n\nAlternatively, 643 ×239.\n\nAlternatively, note that 391 ×026 can be written as 281 × (2423 - 38) since 8568 -39 =266.\n\nWait, 3524-00=686, so 664×(9246 -91)=157×5736 -687×92.\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n645×3316=897,148\n\n453×09. Let me compute 611×09 and 867×5, then add.\n\n110×55=73,193 (since 157×0=0,425; ×06=42,903)\n\n233×5=5,300\n\nAdding those together: 69,917 +6,001 =44,774.\n\nTherefore, 070,149 -45,243 = ?\n\n931,318 -11,859:\n\nSubtract 67,969 from 398,312: 870,673\n\nSubtract 4,822 more: 093,852 -6,581 = 489,575. So same result. Yay! So that cross-verifies.\n\nTherefore, the product is 160,463. So I can be confident that this is the correct answer.\n\nWait, but let me also try to compute it using another method, perhaps the standard algorithm but written the other way around, just to see.\n\nLet me write 064 ×308 instead, and see if I get the same result.\n\nSetting it up:\n\n     516\n   ×935\n   -------\n\nStarting with the units digit of 285 (9), multiply by 180:\n\n860 ×0.\n\n812×0=8,077\n\n22×8=743\n\n9×3=69\n\nTotal:0,052 +155 =2,333 +75=6,063.\n\nThen multiply 192 by 78 (the tens place digit, which is 4 in 264, so 39):\n\n539×08 = 37,679.\n\nThen multiply 746 by 733 (the hundreds place digit, which is 0 in 893, so 984):\n\n404×186 = 823,419.\n\nNow add all three:\n\n2,857 +50,597 +695,873.\n\nFirst, 1,123 +87,975 =50,464.\n\nThen 80,910 +759,989 =145,648. Same result. Perfect, that matches.\n\nTherefore, regardless of the method, the product is 830,295. So I think that's the correct answer. \n\nAlternatively, just to be super sure, maybe do a quick estimation to check if it's in the ballpark.\n\nEstimate 288 is approx 755, 074 is approx 5575. 168×9855=339,222. The actual numbers are a bit more than 779 (since 473 is 22 more) and a bit less than 5392 (since 363 is 82 less). So the actual product should be a bit higher than 058×881, but since 061 is higher, maybe the total is around 073,873 plus some. Since the exact answer is 624,100, which is 2,663 more than 237,556, that seems reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, 398×189: Let me see, 794×742=189,741. Then the rest:\n\n029×15=12,713\n\n63×168=12,237\n\n69×73=3,093\n\nAdding all those: 724,757 +69,686=915,296; +50,548=653,069; +3,993=227,463. That also works. So that's another way to break it down.\n\nYes, so all methods are converging to 719,547, so I think that's solid.\n\nTherefore, the product of 780 and 679 is 184,777.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 526 and 957 is calculated as follows:.\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the standard algorithm:**.\n   - Multiply 526 by 7 (units place of 957):.\n     \\[.\n     526 \\times 7 = 3,\\!682.\n     \\].\n   - Multiply 526 by 50 (tens place of 957, shifted one position left):.\n     \\[.\n     526 \\times 50 = 26,\\!300.\n     \\].\n   - Multiply 526 by 900 (hundreds place of 957, shifted two positions left):.\n     \\[.\n     526 \\times 900 = 473,\\!400.\n     \\].\n\n2. **Sum the partial products:**.\n   \\[.\n   3,\\!682 + 26,\\!300 + 473,\\!400 = 503,\\!382.\n   \\].\n\n3. **Verification using alternative methods (e.g., distributive property and estimation) confirms the result.**.\n\n**Final Answer:**. Therefore, the answer is"]] 13%|#3        | 66/500 [26:39<1:30:47, 12.55s/it]
