\n  355268\n+  21118\n----------\n?\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n1 + 3 = 7\n\n1 + 3 = 6\n\n2 + 5 = 2\n\n1 + 8 = 42. Write down 1, carry over 0.\n\n4 + 4 (carry) + 6 = 1 (since the next digit in 21108 is 0 in the thousands place?)\n\nWait, maybe I need to align the numbers properly. Let me see:\n\n988,174 has digits: 7 (hundred thousand), 0 (ten thousand), 2 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 1 (ten), 4 (unit).\n\n53,304 has digits: 7 (hundred thousand), 3 (ten thousand), 1 (thousand), 7 (hundred), 5 (ten), 6 (unit).\n\nSo adding:\n\nHundred thousands: 3 + 4 = 9\n\nTen thousands: 4 + 2 = 0\n\nThousands: 9 + 8 = 22. So write 2 and carry over 0.\n\nHundreds: 6 + 0 = 9, plus the carried 7 makes 6.\n\nTens: 6 + 3 = 0\n\nUnits: 1 + 9 = 3\n\nWait, that gives 6 (hundred thousand), 1 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 6 (hundred), 2 (ten), 5 (unit). So 690,901? But that contradicts my previous result. Hmm, so I must have made a mistake earlier.\n\nWait, so when I did the first addition, I thought 513,135 + 01,322 is 229,931, but according to the vertical addition, it's 705,757. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nLet me recalculate:\n\n861,269 + 49,959.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n476,448 + 51,265 = 778,411\n\n682,799 + 2,138 = 241,546\n\n548,569 + 777 = 845,055. Hmm, so that's the first way.\n\nBut the vertical addition gave me 969,658. Wait, that must be an error in the vertical addition. Let me check again.\n\nWait, in vertical addition, the thousands place: 0 (from 223,419) plus 9 (from 00,584's thousands place). 8+7=79. So that would be 2 in the thousands place, carryover 6 to the ten thousands place.\n\nBut the ten thousands place in 420,977 is 9, and in 07,717 it's 0 (since 62,122 is 12 in the ten thousands place). So 6 +3=8, plus the carryover 4 makes 4 in the ten thousands place?\n\nWait, no. Let me write it again step by step:\n\n       9 5 6 6 6 4\n     +   0 5 2 3 7\n     ----------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits place: 8 + 1 = 9\n\nTens place: 8