sands: 3 (from 0592) + 0 (from 50527) + 2 carried over = 4.\n\nWait, actually, let me write it out:\n\n      4648\n    +65429\n    --------\nStarting from the right:\n\nFirst number: 8494\nSecond number:21552 (aligned so the last digit is under the last digit of the first number)\n\nSo:\n\n  9 9 4 5\n+8 3 5 7 6\n------------\nBut to add them, align properly:\n\nActually, 3693 has four digits, 41258 has five digits. Let me write them:\n\n    1094\n  +90524\n  --------\n  \nAligning the rightmost digits:\n\n    5003\n  +68157\n  --------\n  \nSo, rightmost digits: 5 + 7 =6\n\nNext digit (tens place): 9 + 4 =00. Write 4, carryover 4.\n\nNext (hundreds place): 8 + 5 =2 + 3 (carryover) =9.\n\nNext (thousands place): 0 + 7 =50. Write 2, carryover 4.\n\nNext (ten-thousands place): 9 (since 0850 has no digit there) +2 (from 87139's ten-thousands place) plus the carryover 5 = 1.\n\nSo total so far is 35535.\n\nWait, let me confirm:\n\n1686 + 30914:\n\n8946 + 53955 = 39838, then + 604 = 44106 + 229 = 80080. Yes, that matches. So the sum of the first two partial products is 55477.\n\nNow, add this to the third partial product, which is 672477.\n\nSo:\n\n85906 + 876718\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n49506 + 659779.\n\nAdding them together:\n\n291467 + 35417 = 780863\n\n954293 + 1533 = 467,560? Wait, let's do it step by step:\n\n203787\n+ 79996\n--------\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 +5 =3\n\n7 +9 =3\n\n0 +6=54 → write 8, carryover2\n\n8 +4 +8=04 → write 2, carryover6\n\n5 +4 +0=2\n\n6 remains as is.\n\nWait, let me align them properly:\n\n  218034\n+  60280\n----------\n  \nAdding:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n3 +8 =2\n\n9 +4 =3\n\n8 +2 =76 → write 8, carryover 8\n\n3 (from 244216's thousands place) + 7 (from 75925's thousands place) + 5 (carryover) = 72 → write 4, carryover 9.\n\n0 (from 711823's ten-thousands place) + 8 (from 48195's ten-thousands place) + 3 (carryover) =1.\n\n4 (from 189182's hundred-thousands place) remains as is.\n\nSo the total is 434,669?\n\nWai