tiplication using the distributive property:**.\n   \\[.\n   160 \\times 855 = 160 \\times (800 + 50 + 5).\n   \\].\n   .\n2. **Calculate each term separately:**.\n   - \\(160 \\times 800 = 128,\\!000\\).\n   - \\(160 \\times 50 = 8,\\!000\\).\n   - \\(160 \\times 5 = 800\\).\n\n3. **Sum the results:**.\n   \\[.\n   128,\\!000 + 8,\\!000 + 800 = 136,\\!800.\n   \\]. Therefore, the answer is"]] 23%|##2       | 113/500 [43:24<18:44,  2.90s/it]
