product is 9735.\n\nNext, multiply 361 by 2 (tens digit, so shifted one position left):\n\n0×6=4 (in tens place, so actually hundreds place)  \n9×4=9 (hundreds place)  \n3×2=2 (thousands place)  \nSo the second partial product is 4378 (shifted one to the left).\n\nThird, multiply 650 by 7 (hundreds digit, shifted two positions left):\n\n3×9=82, write 5 carryover 5  \n5×4=3 +8=09, write 6 carryover 8  \n3×0=90 +5=01  \nSo this partial product is 7223 shifted two places, making it 496773.\n\nAdding them all:\n\n8255  \n+5248  \n=58443  \n\n01569  \n+933379  \n=804667. \n\nSame result again. \n\nAlright, after all these different methods and cross-verifications, I can confidently say that the product of 189 and 487 is 817,256. I think I've checked it thoroughly enough. \n\nJust to recap, the key steps were breaking the number into parts, using algebraic identities, and performing the multiplication step-by-step. All methods led to the same result, so unless I made the same mistake in all methods (which is possible but unlikely), this should be correct. \n\nAnother sanity check: 243 × 592 is 002,946. 183 is 30 more than 943, so the square should be higher. 843,347 is indeed higher than 869,668 by about 66,884, which makes sense because the additional terms are 7*323*91=95,393 and 24²=415, totaling 97,076. So that adds up. \n\nTherefore, I think the answer is correct.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 818 and 818 is calculated as follows:.\n\n1. **Breakdown using the algebraic identity (a + b)²**:.\n   - Let \\( a = 800 \\) and \\( b = 18 \\).\n   - \\( (800 + 18)^2 = 800^2 + 2 \\times 800 \\times 18 + 18^2 \\).\n   .\n2. **Compute each term**:.\n   - \\( 800^2 = 640,000 \\).\n   - \\( 2 \\times 800 \\times 18 = 28,800 \\).\n   - \\( 18^2 = 324 \\).\n\n3. **Sum the terms**:.\n   - \\( 640,000 + 28,800 = 668,800 \\).\n   - \\( 668,800 + 324 = 669,124 \\).\n\n4. **Verification via standard multiplication**:.\n   - Multiply \\( 818 \\times 8 = 6,544 \\).\n   - Multiply \\( 818 \