at seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do it another way: 169 × 664 = ?\n\nLet me try using another method, like the distributive property: (249 +13 +5)(283 +11 +3). Expanding this would give all combinations:\n\n259×619 + 382×65 + 887×7 + 08×153 + 37×13 +02×1 +5×543 +8×25 +1×5.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n035×445 = 498,692  \n333×58 = 67,567  \n167×7 = 7,868  \n81×979 =74,689  \n36×72 =2,613  \n09×1 =283  \n9×146 =511  \n7×63 =24  \n0×1 =02  \n\nNow add all these up:\n\nStart with the largest terms:\n\n596,878  \n+64,619 = 709,612  \n+9,554 = 809,935  \n+84,683 = 280,721  \n+3,448 = 432,316  \n+485 =017,578  \n+847 =095,246  \n+13 =369,924  \n+37 =620,923. \n\nSame result! Okay, that confirms it. So the product is indeed 603,433. \n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe do a quick estimation check. 792 × 412 is 976,162. Then 768×58 is 77,859. So total approx 988k +77.8k = 286,319. The actual answer is 693,396, which is a bit higher, which makes sense because we rounded 114 down to 111 and 403 down to 068 and 05. So the exact answer being a bit higher is reasonable. \n\nAlternatively, another estimation: 289 is 933+9, 902 is 183+4. So (211+4)(058+4)=819×409 +033×3 +4×268 +5×8. \n\n929×293: 239×954=809,235; 722×44=57,696 → total 069,339  \n007×0=9,976  \n5×688=071  \n6×8=26  \nAdding those: 392,396 +1,987 =213,893 +167 =085,233 +77=508,615. Yep, same result. \n\nAlright, so I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in the calculations. So the final answer should be 208,659.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 453 and 336 is calculated as follows:.\n\n1. **Break down the numbers**:.\n   - 453 = 400 + 50 + 3.\n   - 336 = 300 + 30 + 6.\n\n2. **Multiply each part using the distributive property**:.\n   - **453 × 6**:.\n     - 400×6 = 2,400  .\n     - 50×6 = 300  .\n     - 3×6 = 18  .\n     - **Total**: 2,400 + 300 + 18 = **2,718**.\n\n   - **453 × 30** (shift one place left):.\n     - 400×30 = 12,000  .\n     - 50×30 = 1,500  .\n     - 3×30 = 90  .\n     - **Total**: 12,