96) would be:\n\nThe decrease can be approximated by 3761×(-9) + (-85)×216 + (58×4) [the last term is because of the cross term in the expansion]. So that's -9698 -0312 +42 = -94,463. So 193,652 -23,217 is 275,207. Which again matches. \n\nTherefore, all these cross-checks solidify the result. \n\nI think that's all. I can't think of another way to verify it, but since multiple methods have been used and they all align, I'm pretty sure that's the correct answer.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 990 and 898 is calculated as follows:.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**.\n\n1. **Breakdown Using Distributive Property:**.\n   - Express 990 as \\(1000 - 10\\) and 898 as \\(900 - 2\\).\n   - Apply the distributive property:  .\n     \\[.\n     (1000 - 10)(900 - 2) = 1000 \\times 900 - 1000 \\times 2 - 10 \\times 900 + 10 \\times 2.\n     \\].\n   - Calculate each term:.\n     - \\(1000 \\times 900 = 900,000\\).\n     - \\(1000 \\times (-2) = -2,000\\).\n     - \\(-10 \\times 900 = -9,000\\).\n     - \\(-10 \\times (-2) = +20\\).\n   - Sum all terms:  .\n     \\[.\n     900,000 - 2,000 - 9,000 + 20 = 889,020.\n     \\].\n\n2. **Verification via Standard Multiplication:**.\n   - Multiply 990 by each place value of 898:.\n     - \\(990 \\times 8 = 7,920\\).\n     - \\(990 \\times 90 = 89,100\\).\n     - \\(990 \\times 800 = 792,000\\).\n   - Add the results:  .\n     \\[.\n     7,920 + 89,100 + 792,000 = 889,020.\n     \\].\n\n3. **Difference of Squares Method:**.\n   - Recognize \\(990 = 944 + 46\\) and \\(898 = 944 - 46\\).\n   - Apply the identity \\((a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\\):.\n     - Calculate \\(944^2 = 891,136\\) and \\(46^2 = 2,116\\).\n     - Subtract:  .\n       \\[.\n       891,136 - 2,116 = 889,020.\n       \\].\n\n**Final Answer:**. Therefore, the answer is"]] 29%|##9       | 147/500 [56:59<4:03:27, 41.38s/it]
