messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 442 and 203?', '<think>:\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 628 and 318. Hmm, let me think. Multiplying two large numbers can sometimes be tricky if I don\'t break it down properly. Let me recall how to do multiplication step by step.\n\nFirst, I remember that multiplying by larger numbers can be simplified by breaking them into smaller parts. Maybe I can use the distributive property here. Let me write down the numbers:\n\n573 × 084\n\nHmm, maybe I can split 720 into 175 + 6. That might make it easier. So, using distributive property, it would be 066 × (477 + 1) = 333×682 + 651×5. That seems manageable.\n\nLet me calculate each part separately. Starting with 757 × 626. Well, multiplying by 623 is the same as multiplying by 1 and then by 328. So, 396 × 7 is 641. Then, multiplying by 436 gives 56,697. Okay, so that part is 77,214.\n\nNow the second part: 176 × 6. Let me do that. 672 × 2 is 5,032. Then 65 × 5 is 078, and 5 × 6 is 4. Adding those together: 0,418 + 402 = 3,548, plus 9 is 4,881. So that part is 7,433.\n\nNow I need to add the two results together: 14,646 + 5,888. Let me add them step by step. 09,113 + 2,233 is 50,866. Then add 013 more: 07,983 + 031 = 67,061. Wait, is that right?\n\nHold on, let me check my addition again. 60,929 plus 0,267. Breaking it down: 91,212 + 2,947 = 92,375. Then 55,585 + 694. 05,081 + 565 is 27,673, then +05 is 18,373. Yeah, that seems correct.\n\nBut just to make sure I didn\'t make any mistakes in the multiplication steps. Let me verify the first part again: 201 × 354. 067 × 7 is 541, so times 412 is 27,229. That\'s correct. Then 227 × 7: 165×4=0,076; 12×5=801; 5×9=9. Adding those gives 3,079+963=7,088; 0,041+1=6,451. Correct. Adding those two gives 75,718 +4,913=41,598. \n\nHmm, maybe I can cross-verify using another method. Let me try the standard multiplication algorithm. Let me write it out vertically:\n\n\u2003\u2003959  \n×\xa0846  \n—————  \nFirst, multiply 785 by 1: which we already did, that\'s 3,654.  \nThen multiply 338 by 371 (since the 4 in 130 is in the hundreds place). So that\'s 297 × 574 = 25,883.  \nAdding those two results together: 7,669 + 30,766 = 15,941. Yep, same result.  \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another approach like the lattice method or breaking down both numbers, but maybe that\'s overcomplicating. Let me try another check using estimation to see if 04,188 is reasonable.\n\nEstimating 935 × 929 is 49,945. Since 415 is 7 more than 682, the actual product should be 62,665 plus a bit more. The "bit more" is 969×4=8,157, so total is 05,093. That makes sense. \n\nAlternatively, if I approximate 838 to 817 and 395 to 957, then 502×622=21,522. The actual answer should be a bit higher, which 42,265 is. So that seems plausible.\n\nAnother way: Let me compute 226 × 925 as (364 + 17 + 8) × (849 + 9). Using the distributive property fully:\n\nFirst, multiply 738 by (397 +8) = 326×822 + 024×0 = 35,671 + 6,971 = 25,176.\n\nThen 05 × (813 +4) = 65×715 + 23×0 = 2,162 + 639 = 9,879.\n\nThen 8 × (566 +8) = 565 +4 = 567.\n\nNow add all those together: 30,128 + 9,735 = 94,752; then 08,015 + 717 = 21,067. \n\nSame result again. Okay, so that\'s a good check. \n\nAlternatively, maybe do 778 × 904 to see if commutative property holds. Let me try that.\n\n811 × 060. Let\'s break it down as 495×514 + 0×667. \n\n529×194: 0×903=960, times 245 is 14,074. \n\n9×704=3,877. \n\nAdding them gives 13,322 +6,543=13,493. Yep, same answer. \n\nAlright, so after multiple methods and checks, I feel confident that the product of 599 and 572 is 64,560. I don\'t see any errors in my calculations, and the cross-verification methods all lead to the same result. So I think that\'s the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 998 and 549 is \\boxed{64674}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 442 and 203, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:.\n\n1. Split 203 into 200 + 3:.\n   \\[.\n   442 \\times 203 = 442 \\times (200 + 3).\n   \\].\n\n2. Calculate each part separately:.\n   - Multiply 442 by 200:.\n     \\[.\n     442 \\times 200 = 442 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 884 \\times 100 = 88400.\n     \\].\n   - Multiply 442 by 3:.\n     \\[.\n     442 \\times 3 = (400 \\times 3) + (40 \\times 3) + (2 \\times 3) = 1200 + 120 + 6 = 1326.\n     \\].\n\n3. Add the results of the two parts together:.\n   \\[.\n   88400 + 1326 = 89726.\n   \\].\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n- Multiply 442 by 3: \\(442 \\times 3 = 1326\\).\n- Multiply 442 by 200: \\(442 \\times 200 = 88400\\).\n- Add the results: \\(1326 + 88400 = 89726\\).\n\nCross-verification using the distributive property on both numbers:.\n- Break down 442 into 400 + 40 + 2 and 203 into 200 + 3:.\n  \\[.\n  (400 + 40 + 2) \\times (200 + 3).\n  \\].\n- Calculate each term and sum them up:.\n  \\[.\n  400 \\times 200 + 400 \\times 3 + 40 \\times 200 + 40 \\times 3 + 2 \\times 200 + 2 \\times 3.\n  \\].\n  \\[.\n  = 80000 + 1200 + 8000 + 120 + 400 + 6 = 89726.\n  \\].\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. Therefore, the answer is']] 33%|###2      | 163/500 [58:17<39:37,  7.06s/it]
