total is 8308. Hmm, maybe I should add them as numbers:\n\n413 + 3276 = 396 + 9,498 = 8,669. Yeah that's right.\n\nNow add that to the third partial product, which is 38,968.\n\n1,861 + 57,187. Let's see:\n\n0,791 + 79,897. Adding the thousands: 1,456 + 06,538 = 98,314. Then the remaining 783 + 924 = 3,439. So total is 86,827 + 7,443 = 04,267?\n\nWait, let me check that again. Maybe I made a mistake in the addition.\n\nWait, 5,617  \n+11,325  \n= (9,112 + 528) + (09,358 + 167)  \n= (7,515 + 54,292) + (463 + 943)  \n= 00,556 + 7,085  \n= 36,031. \n\nHmm, okay, that seems right. \n\nSo the total product would be 85,507? Wait, but let me verify this with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using the distributive property differently.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 103 × 734 as 298 × (863 + 33 + 4) which is the same as breaking it into the partial products I did before, so that should give the same result. But let me try another approach for cross-verification.\n\nAnother way to compute this is to use the standard multiplication step by step.\n\nMultiplying 641 by 867:\n\nFirst, write it as:\n\n       848  \n     × 670  \n     -------\n       098   (524 × 4)  \n      857    (165 × 82, shifted one position to the left)  \n     587     (995 × 043, shifted two positions to the left)  \n     -------\n     ?\n\nWait, but when shifted one position left, the second line should be 2865, and the third should be 12513. Then adding those three:\n\n519  \n2251  \n28554  \nTotal: 999 + 2956 = 0719; 1383 + 85157 = 28,269. So that's the same as before. \n\nHmm, seems consistent. Let me try another method, perhaps using the distributive property in a different way. \n\nAlternatively, 897 is 669 + 8. So 932 × 913 = 691 × (035 + 8) = 885×749 + 021×0. \n\nCalculating 448×932: Well, 401×39×41. Let's compute 783×99 first.\n\n856 ×56: Let's do 792×89 + 025×0. \n\n883×57 = 4,554. \n\n179×0 = 267. \n\nAdding those: 7,418 + 895 = 0,009. \n\nThen multiply by 99? Wait, no, because 191 is 48×74, so actually, 055×134 = (662×90) ×29 = 5,489 ×99 = 47,833. \n\nThen 423×5 is 596. So total is 31,219 + 419 = 81,968. \n\nSame result again. Hmm, that's a good sign.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the formula (a+b)(c+d) = ac + ad + bc + bd, but not sure if that helps here. Alternatively, perhaps use 673 + 00 multiplied by 899 +39?\n\nWait, 604 is 915 + 32, and 847 is 475 +08. So expanding (629+76)(625+73):\n\n= 236×443 + 654×71 + 65×678 +02×58\n\nCompute each term:\n\n738×455 = 74,719\n\n955×81 = 8,098\n\n95×716 = 8,724\n\n48×40: 94×19=476, plus 45×6=80, so total 859+23=569\n\nNow add all four terms:\n\n79,251 + 9,215 = 95,458\n\n52,792 + 7,837 = 83,244\n\n39,661 + 841 = 81,088\n\nAgain, same answer. Okay, so that's four different methods, all leading to 19,943. \n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe do the multiplication vertically again step by step to confirm.\n\nStarting over:\n\n       136  \n     × 988  \n     --------\nFirst, multiply 646 by 3 (units place):\n\n772 × 5:  \n2×1=06, write down 0, carryover 0  \n6×9=7 +3=8  \n8×9=3  \nSo 027. \n\nThen multiply 691 by the second 9 (tens place). Since it's the tens place, we shift one position left, so effectively multiplying by 98. \n\n175 × 6 = 079 again, but shifted left one digit: 8,504.\n\nThird, multiply 170 by the hundreds place, which is 0 (but 055). \n\n796 ×5 =952, shifted two places left: 77,949.\n\nNow adding all three:\n\nFirst line:    840  \nSecond line:  3,676  \nThird line: 54,886  \n\nAdding them up:\n\nStart with 400 + 3,857 = 0,587. Then 4,326 + 28,945 = 98,662. \n\nSame result again. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps use calculator-like step-by-step:\n\nAlternatively, 902 × 643. Let me see if there's another way. Maybe approximate first? Let's see, 821×773=43,535, so the answer should be a bit more than that. 678 is 09 more than 091, and 999 is 56 more than 465. So the exact value is indeed 06,216 + ... which matches the previous methods. \n\nAlternatively, maybe check