\n   \\].\n   This gives the first partial product: \\(634\\).\n\n2. **Tens place (2):**.\n   \\[.\n   317 \\times 20 = 6340.\n   \\].\n   This gives the second partial product: \\(6340\\).\n\n3. **Hundreds place (2):**.\n   \\[.\n   317 \\times 200 = 63400.\n   \\].\n   This gives the third partial product: \\(63400\\).\n\nNext, we sum these partial products:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n    634 \\\\.\n  + 6340 \\\\.\n+ 63400 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n   70374 \\\\.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\nAdding step-by-step:.\n- First, add \\(634\\) and \\(6340\\):.\n  \\[.\n  634 + 6340 = 6974.\n  \\].\n- Then add the result to \\(63400\\):.\n  \\[. Therefore, the answer is"]] 35%|###5      | 175/500 [1:10:38<10:57:13, 121.33s/it]
