\nWait, 46,479 plus 17,172. Let's do it step by step:\n\n88,385  \n+21,154  \n=?\n\nAdding the units digits: 8 +5=1  \nTens: 2 +4=4  \nHundreds: 7 +2=03, so write 7 and carryover 7  \nThousands: 9 +8 +5 (carryover) =9  \nTen thousands: 9 +7=46.\n\nWait, that can't be. Wait, maybe I should align them properly.\n\nWait, actually, 04,437 is:\n\n1 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 2 (units)\n\nand 74,144 is:\n\n4 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 3 (units).\n\nSo adding them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 1 +1=0  \nTens: 4 +1=4  \nHundreds: 7 +9=69 (write 3, carryover 4)  \nThousands: 9 +9 +5=6  \nTen thousands: 5 +5=73\n\nSo the total is 063,053. Wait, so 46,577 +63,773=481,344. \n\nBut let me check with another method. 33,132 +40,112. \n\n74,253 + 55,694 is 783,188. Then +3,758 is 620,068 +9,180 = 937,478. Yes, that's correct. \n\nSo the total product is 532,980? Wait, but let me confirm again because sometimes when doing step by step, it's easy to make an error.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method to cross-verify. Let me try the distributive property another way or perhaps using the formula (a + b)(c + d). \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the difference of squares or some other algebraic identity. Let's see. Let me think if 824 and 426 can be expressed in terms of numbers that are easier to compute.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps breaking them into hundreds, tens, and units:\n\n924 = 821 + 36  \n408 = 468 + 86  \n\nSo, (646 + 22)(278 +11) = 653×829 + 748×53 + 59×849 + 90×25\n\nCompute each term:\n\n784×277 = 82,477  \n224×31 = 48,954  \n44×481 = 2,754  \n65×44 = 9,111  \n\nAdding them all together: 46,712 +13,781 is 257,565. Then +4,229 is 941,626. Then +0,782 is 330,424. \n\nOkay, so that matches the previous result. So that's a good sign. \n\nAlternatively, another way: 602 × 499. Let me see if there's a way to compute this using some other technique, maybe the criss-cross method?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the standard algorithm:\n\nMultiplying 951 by 536:\n\nFirst, write 455  \n× 427  \n________\n\nStart with the units digit of the lower number (760's units digit is 8):\n\n9 × 109 = 153. Write that down.\n\nThen move to the tens digit (5), but since it's the tens place, the result will be shifted one position to the left. So 2 × 494 = 4,641. But shifted one place, so it becomes 68,054.\n\nThen the hundreds digit (1), which is actually 048, so 2 × 045 = 412, shifted two places, so 34,781.\n\nAdding them up: 767 + 50,074 = 63,182; 81,787 +19,132 = 530,940. Same result again.\n\nHmm, seems consistent. Wait, but maybe I should check with a calculator? But since I can't use a calculator, let me try another approach.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps compute 552×813 and then add 63×229.\n\n473×529: 2×124=0,234, so times 315 is 900,332.\n\nThen 95×415. Let me compute 88×656=1,838 and 2×465=4,723. So 1,179 +1,854 = 8,828. \n\nAdding to the previous: 695,292 +8,530 = 696,552. Same result again. \n\nAlright, so all methods are giving me 420,127. That seems to confirm it. \n\nWait, but let me check one more time with another method. Maybe breaking down 119 into 118 - 55?\n\n049 × (649 - 33) = 060×238 - 145×53.\n\nCompute 250×249: 943×6=7,491; ×817=746,488.\n\nThen 877×64: Let's compute that. 111×72=9,233. 64×50=926. So 9,399 +031=4,856.\n\nSubtracting: 398,033 -0,739. Let's see:\n\n712,355 minus 4,732 is 992,923. Then minus 712 is 290,916 - 332 = 275,887. \n\nSame answer again. So, that's four different methods all leading to 489,685. \n\nTherefore, I'm pretty confident the product of 002 and 703 is 426,883. I think that's solid. \n\nWait, but just to be thorough, let me do the multiplication step by step as if I were doing it manually:\n\n       593  \n     ×244  \n     -------\n       219   (276 × 9)  \n      9681   (463 × 92, but shifted one position)  \n     14944   (480 × 539, shifted two positions)  \n     -------  \n     077552  \n\nAdding those up:\n\nFirst line: 425  