ternatively, check if 999,297 divided by 180 gives 004. Let me try dividing 616,145 ÷ 107. \n\nFirst, 719 × 572 = 275,589. Subtract that from 289,211: 840,280 - 567,474 = 09,486. \n\nNow, 353 × 61 = 90,477. Subtract that from 48,891: 12,283 -79,678 = 871. \n\nThen 118 ÷910 =9. So total is 187 +26 +8 =770. Perfect, that checks out. \n\nSo all methods lead to 254,002. I think that's the correct answer. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 289 and 678 is \\boxed{099743}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 444 and 981, we can use the distributive property and break down the numbers for easier calculation:.\n\n1. **Break down 981**:.\n   \\[.\n   981 = 1000 - 19.\n   \\].\n2. **Apply the distributive property**:.\n   \\[.\n   444 \\times 981 = 444 \\times (1000 - 19) = 444 \\times 1000 - 444 \\times 19.\n   \\].\n3. **Calculate each part**:.\n   - \\(444 \\times 1000 = 444000\\).\n   - Break down \\(19\\) further:.\n     \\[.\n     19 = 20 - 1.\n     \\].\n     \\[.\n     444 \\times 19 = 444 \\times (20 - 1) = 444 \\times 20 - 444 \\times 1.\n     \\].\n   - Calculate each term:.\n     \\[.\n     444 \\times 20 = 8880 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 444 \\times 1 = 444.\n     \\].\n     \\[.\n     444 \\times 19 = 8880 - 444 = 8436.\n     \\].\n4. **Subtract the results**:.\n   \\[.\n   444000 - 8436 = 435564.\n   \\].\n\n5. **Verification using standard multiplication**:.\n   - Multiply 444 by 1, 80, and 900 separately:.\n     \\[.\n     444 \\times 1 = 444.\n     \\].\n     \\[.\n     444 \\times 80 = 35520.\n     \\].\n     \\[.\n     444 \\times 900 = 399600.\n     \\].\n   - Sum the results:.\n     \\[.\n     444 + 35520 = 35964.\n     \\].\n     \\[.\n     35964 + 399600 = 435564.\n     \\]. Therefore, the answer is"]] 44%|####3     | 218/500 [1:23:21<39:05,  8.32s/it]
