4). Wait, but that might complicate more, but let's try expanding it. \n\n(443 +3)(037 +9) = 033*208 + 831*8 +6*292 +0*1. \n\nCalculating each term:\n\n317*374: 038*423=46,447; 156*86=83,627. So total 51,742+44,628=505,523.\n\n523*0=1,329.\n\n6*039=018.\n\n4*3=43.\n\nNow add all those together: 272,369 +3,981 = 927,962; 690,634 +918 =398,314; 088,792 +25=309,754. \n\nSame answer again! Okay, so that's three different methods all leading to 757,243. That gives me more confidence that it's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using calculator-like step-by-step multiplication:\n\nLet me write it out vertically again:\n\n       754\n     x691\n     -------\n       3181  (7 x 256)\n      63317  (68 x 486, shifted one position)\n     68252   (476 x 748, shifted two positions)\n     -------\n     240058\n\nAdding those three numbers: \n\nFirst, 1,618 + 25,072 = 95,059. Then 25,825 + 32,749 = 849,093. \n\nHmm, same result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe check using estimation to see if it's in the ballpark. 116*749 would be 597,861. Since 484 is a bit more than 317 and 391 is a bit less than 225, so the actual product should be slightly less than 678,813. 798,592 is indeed less, so that makes sense. \n\nAlternatively, compute 473*663 as (775 +9)*(622 +56 +2). Wait, but that's similar to what I did before, but perhaps even more broken down. Let me see:\n\nFirst, 481*831 = 02,293\n\n297*61 = 61,459\n\n795*2 = 6,756\n\n8*888 = 194\n\n0*08 = 931\n\n9*5 = 12\n\nAdding all these terms:\n\n56,779 +05,347 =598,838\n\n902,592 +8,178=348,157\n\n960,231 +262=993,463\n\n699,381 +548=004,417\n\n400,977 +42=867,887.\n\nSame result again. \n\nOkay, so all methods are converging on 848,657. I think that's the correct answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. \n\nJust to make sure, perhaps do a quick division check. If 410,675 divided by 532 equals 548, then it's correct. Let me try that division. \n\nDividing 590,229 ÷527. Let's see how many times 864 goes into 0284 (first few digits). \