(from 82,419) +8 =6\n\nThousands place:6 +3 =8\n\nHundreds place:5 +0 =55\n\nTens place:0 +2=72\n\nOnes place:5 +1=5\n\nWait but with the carryovers:\n\nWait let me do it properly:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 1 +2 =3\n\nTens place:1 (from 9,523) +5 (from 67,974) =54. Write down 9, carryover 2.\n\nHundreds place:2 (from 0,485) +9 (from 62,639) =89, plus the carried 0 =83. Write down 9, carryover 2.\n\nThousands place:6 (from 3,435) +1 (from 26,234) =0, plus the carried 4 =9.\n\nTen-thousands place:2 (from 3,210) +0 (from 76,549) =0.\n\nSo the total is 99,713. Correct. Then adding that to 468,617:\n\n67,573 +157,327 =507,481. Yep, that's the same as before.\n\nAnother way, perhaps using another distributive approach:\n\n996 *638 =322*(845+47)=316*512 +711*38.\n\nWe already know 997*181=349,794.\n\nNow compute 866*53:\n\n294*04 +320*1 =25,277 +9,782 =63,975.\n\nThen total is 383,899 +72,517 =741,879. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 301*840 as (328 -63)*(387 +43) which we did earlier, and that also gave 092,433. So all methods converge to that number.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the answer is 852,926.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 321 and 500 is \\boxed{826794}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 689 and 922, we can break down the multiplication using the distributive property and then sum the results.\n\nFirst, we break down 922 into 900, 20, and 2:.\n\\[.\n689 \\times 922 = 689 \\times (900 + 20 + 2).\n\\].\n\nNext, we calculate each part separately:.\n1. \\(689 \\times 900\\):.\n   \\[.\n   689 \\times 9 = 6201 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 6201 \\times 100 = 620100.\n   \\].\n2. \\(689 \\times 20\\):.\n   \\[.\n   689 \\times 2 = 1378 \\quad \\text{(then add one zero)} \\quad 1378 \\times 10 = 13780.\n   \\].\n3. \\(689 \\times 2\\):.\n   \\[.\n   689 \\times 2 = 1378.\n   \\].\n\nNow, we sum the results of the three parts:.\n\\[.\n620100 + 13780 + 1378.\n\\].\n\nAdding these step-by-step:.\n1. \\(620100 + 13780 = 633