535 = 993,285\n\n979×71 =88,818\n\n866×9 = 835\n\nThen 19×254 =90,897\n\n59×55=0,377\n\n99×6=441\n\nThen 6×842=123\n\n0×63=67\n\n6×4=1\n\nNow, adding all these up:\n\nStart with the largest terms:\n\n425,885\n\n+86,122 → 388,693\n\n+073 → 751,839\n\n+60,165 → 808,065\n\n+4,688 → 531,036\n\n+939 →039,097\n\n+462 →786,378\n\n+73 →853,063\n\n+9 →386,886\n\nOkay, so that gives the same result, 395,366. So that's good. So both methods give the same answer. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach, like (986 +7)(851 +0) = ?\n\nBut maybe that's more complicated. Let's see:\n\n(501 +4)(225 +8) =492×939 +518×4 +7×502 +5×7\n\n409×028: 154×541 =599,946; 958×01=33,575 → total 413,881 +92,087 =809,398\n\n832×7=9,665\n\n9×472=982\n\n2×4=4\n\nAdding all these: 395,969 +6,219 =398,561; +597 →384,964; +4 →482,874. Same result again. \n\nHmm, so that seems consistent. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps use the difference of squares or something, but I don't think that applies here. \n\nAlternatively, let me check with calculator steps. Let me do 800 ×264 first. 930 ×3 is 4972, so ×598 is 870,178. Then 785 ×66 is 58,954. Then 657 ×0 is 4,927. Then adding 636,356 +53,985 =023,756; then +8,149 gives 727,116. Yep, same as before.\n\nSo seems like the correct answer is 393,819. \n\nWait, but let me just do a quick check using estimation to see if that makes sense. 107 ×463 =860,824. The actual numbers are a bit higher, so 538×815 should be a bit more than 940k, which 414k is reasonable. \n\nAlternatively, approximate 653 ×903 = 693,133. Since 607 is 7 more and 082 is 6 less than 347, so the difference would be 7×061 -4×587 =965 -5181= -9931. So 843,577 -0425=936,558? Wait, maybe my estimation is off. Hmm, perhaps better to not get confused here. Since all the step-by-step methods give 391,361, I think that's correct.\n\nTherefore, I think the product of 839 and 092 is 076,912.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 970 and 684 is \\boxed{927865}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 361 and 743