 39080 = 918380.\n     \\].\n\n3. **Standard Long Multiplication**:.\n   - Multiply 977 by each digit of 940 and sum the results:.\n     - Multiply by 0 (units place): \\(977 \\times 0 = 0\\).\n     - Multiply by 4 (tens place): \\(977 \\times 4 = 3908\\), then shift left by 1: \\(39080\\).\n     - Multiply by 9 (hundreds place): \\(977 \\times 9 = 8793\\), then shift left by 2: \\(879300\\).\n     - Sum the partial products:.\n       \\[.\n       39080 + 879300 = 918380.\n       \\].\n\n4. **Alternative Distributive Approach**:.\n   - Express 977 as \\(1000 - 23\\) and compute:.\n     \\[.\n     (1000 - 23) \\times 940 = 1000 \\times 940 - 23 \\times 940.\n     \\].\n   - Calculate each term:.\n     \\[.\n     1000 \\times 940 = 940000, \\quad 23 \\times 940 = 21620.\n     \\].\n   - Combine the results:.\n     \\[.\n     940000 - 21620 = 918380.\n     \\].\n\nAll methods consistently yield the same result. Therefore, the answer is"]] 50%|#####     | 252/500 [1:30:21<1:24:20, 20.40s/it]
