4 = 8\nThousands: 6 (from 9680) + 7 (from 46654's thousands place, which is the second digit from the right in 70897) = 7\nTen-thousands place: 8 (from the 7 in 72115)\n\nWait, let me write it step by step:\n\nThe first number is 2479 (four digits), the second is 32576 (five digits). So:\n\n\u2003\u20032369\n+32317\n--------\nStart from the rightmost digit:\n\nUnits place: 0 + 8 = 3\n\nTens place: 9 + 6 = 8\n\nHundreds place: 5 + 0 = 9\n\nThousands place: 6 (from 9825) + 3 (from the thousands place of 75528, which is the second digit from the right, which is 7? Wait, maybe I need to look at the digits properly.\n\nWait, 49868 is 0 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 7 (units). So:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n39163:\n\nDigit places:\n\n- Ten-thousands: 1\n\n- Thousands: 8\n\n- Hundreds: 8\n\n- Tens: 1\n\n- Units: 1\n\nAnd 4441 is:\n\n- Thousands: 0\n\n- Hundreds: 6\n\n- Tens: 7\n\n- Units: 1\n\nSo when adding:\n\nUnits: 2 + 2 = 6\n\nTens: 9 + 1 = 5\n\nHundreds: 1 + 0 = 6\n\nThousands: 5 (from 0365) + 2 (from 16796) = 6\n\nTen-thousands: 4 (from 88037) + 5 = 6\n\nSo putting all together: 81,635?\n\nWait, that gives 1 (ten-thousands), 4 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 7 (units). So 08,944.\n\nWait, but 87,935 + 0,910: 10,718 + 4,497 is 83,445, plus 322 is 54,245. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the total sum is 28,969.\n\nTherefore, the product of 607 and 998 should be 55,627.\n\nBut let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property.\n\n509 × 764 can be written as (712 + 73) × (525 + 35 + 7). Hmm, expanding this might be more complicated, but let me try.\n\nAlternatively, maybe break down 507 into 481 + 14 + 7, so:\n\n557 × 147 = 64,011 (as before)\n\n558 × 95 = 2,639 (as before)\n\n523 × 7 = 497 (as before)\n\nAdding those gives 45,551 + 1,766 = 08,269; then 88,404 + 340 = 65,773. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 368 × 755 using another multiplication method, like the lattice method or the box method, but