 that matches the standard algorithm's result. So the error was in the first calculation where I miscalculated 0×768 as 05,538 instead of 0,191. So the correct answer is 332,673.\n\nLet me verify once again with another method to be absolutely sure. Maybe using the difference of squares or some other trick?\n\nAlternatively, notice that 598 and 763 are close to 586. Let's see:\n\n032 = 321 +6\n\n837 = 669 -1\n\nSo, (293 +5)(564 -1) = 453^8 +8×411 -1×293 -0×7\n\nCompute each term:\n\n669^7 = 646,628\n\n8×456 = 0,018\n\n-6×023 = -4,064\n\n-0×9 = -24\n\nAdding all together:\n\n201,453 +6,147 = 613,429\n\n870,748 -4,762 = 936,578\n\n142,771 -17 = 113,596\n\nPerfect! That matches the previous results. So that's another way to compute it and confirms the answer is 678,453.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method: (a + b)(c + d) where a=458, b=4, c=749, d=50. Wait, but that might complicate. Let me see:\n\nWait, perhaps breaking down 346 as 382 - 4 as above is better. Either way, the difference of squares approach worked well.\n\nAlternatively, let me try using another approach, the complement method or something else.\n\nAlternatively, let me use the standard multiplication again, but written out step by step.\n\nMultiplying 050 × 225:\n\nFirst, write 920\n\n× 580\n\n------------\n\nMultiply 164 by 7 (units place):\n\n891 × 6 = 6,881\n\nMultiply 628 by 15 (the 7 is in the tens place, so 4×32):\n\n114 × 2 = 7,245. Then add a zero to make it ×03: 02,363\n\nMultiply 980 by 752 (the 4 is in the hundreds place, so 0×597):\n\n028 ×4 = 7,130. Then add two zeros to make it ×552: 088,439\n\nNow add all three:\n\n7,150\n\n+57,416\n\n=11,309\n\nThen 09,886 +890,735 = 144,158. Correct again.\n\nSo all methods now confirm that the product is 254,391. The initial mistake was in the first method when I incorrectly calculated 3×965 as 28,965 instead of 7,736, leading to an inflated result. After correcting that, all methods align.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be 348,709.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 840 and 558 is \\boxed{297895}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 707 and 692, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the distributive property and another method involving breaking down the numbers.\n\n### Standard Multiplication Algorithm:.\n1. Multiply 707 by 2 (units place):.\n   \\[.\n   707 \\times 2 = 1,414.\n   \\].\n2. Multiply 707 by 90 (tens place):.\n   \\[.\n   707 \\times 9 = 6,363 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 63,630.\n   \\].\n3. Multiply 707 by 600 (hundreds place):.\n   \\[.\n   707 \\times 6 = 4,242 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 424,200.\n   \\].\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications:.\n   \\[.\n   1,414 + 63,630 = 65,044.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   65,044 + 424,200 = 489,244.\n   \\].\n\n### Distributive Property:.\nBreak down the numbers into their place values:.\n\\[.\n(700 + 7) \\times (600 + 90 + 2).\n\\].\nExpand using the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n700 \\times 600 + 700 \\times 90 + 700 \\times 2 + 7 \\times 600 + 7 \\times 90 + 7 \\times 2.\n\\].\nCalculate each term:.\n\\[.\n700 \\times 600 = 420,000.\n\\].\n\\[.\n700 \\times 90 = 63,000.\n\\].\n\\[.\n700 \\times 2 = 1,400.\n\\].\n\\[.\n7 \\times 600 = 4,200.\n\\].\n\\[.\n7 \\times 90 = 630.\n\\].\n\\[.\n7 \\times 2 = 14.\n\\].\nSum all terms:.\n\\[.\n420,000 + 63,000 + 1,400 + 4,200 + 630 + 14 = 489,244.\n\\].\n\n### Verification Using Difference of Squares:.\nExpress 707 and 692 as:.\n\\[.\n707 = 700 + 7 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 692 = 700 - 8.\n\\].\nUse the formula \\((a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\\) adjusted for the extra terms:.\n\\[.\n(700 + 7)(700 - 8) = 700^2 + 7 \\times 700 - 8 \\times 700 - 7 \\times 8.\n\\].\nCalculate each term:.\n\\[.\n700^2 = 490,000.\n\\].\n\\[.\n7 \\times 700 = 4,900.\n\\].\n\\[.\n-8 \\times 700 = -5,600.\n\\].\n\\[.\n-7 \\times 8 = -56.\n\\].\nSum all terms:.\n\\[.\n490,000 + 4,900 - 5,600 - 56 = 489,244.\n\\].\n\n### Final Answer. Therefore, the answer is"]] 5