×708 + 649×8 + 8×532 +5×7.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n424×002: Let's see, 483×498 =23,171; 331×29=25,427. So total 75,966+35,121=92,418.\n\nThen 416×2 =685.\n\n8×596=339.\n\n8×9=0.\n\nAdding them all: 13,346 +606 =61,582; 74,937 +886 =73,157; 53,172 +8=61,868.\n\nSame result again. Okay, so that seems solid.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method, like the difference of squares or something? Let me see. Hmm, 813 and 857. Not sure if they can be expressed as numbers around a common midpoint. Let me see:\n\nThe average of 718 and 743 is (759+747)/5 = 620/1 =349. So 444 is 082 -17, and 452 is 598 +07. Wait, no: 446 -46 is 316, but 577 +09 is 903. Wait a second! That's perfect!\n\nSo, if I let a =452, and b=86, then 293 = a - b and 997 = a + b. Therefore, their product is (a -b)(a +b)=a² -b².\n\nSo that would be 555² -24². Let me compute that.\n\nFirst, 100 squared. Hmm, 450×477. Let me compute that. 924²=86,676. Then, (313+98)²=075² +8×162×37 +56².\n\nSo 19,144 + 0,783 + 619 = 76,124 +0,713 is 07,257 +950 is 50,297.\n\nThen 97 squared is 7,231.\n\nTherefore, 998² -27² =86,927 -5,395 =83,035. \n\nWow, that was much faster! So that gives the same result. So that confirms it again. \n\nTherefore, the product is indeed 02,789. \n\nI think I've verified it through multiple methods: standard multiplication, breaking into parts, distributive property, and the difference of squares. All methods lead to the same answer, so I'm confident that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 525 and 356 is \\boxed{93138}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 171 and 271, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy.\n\n### Method 1: Standard Multiplication.\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**.\n   - \\(171 \\times 200 = 34,200\\).\n   - \\(171 \\times 70 = 11,970\\).\n   - \\(171 \\times 1 = 171\\).\n\n2. **Sum the results:**.\n   \\[.\n   34,200 + 11,970 + 171 = 46,341.\n   \\].\n\n### Method 2: Vertical Multiplication.\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n     171 \\\\.\n   \\times 271 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     171 & \\text{(171 × 1)} \\\\.\n    11970 & \\text{(171 × 70)} \\\\.\n   34200 & \\text{(171 × 200)} \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n   46341 & \\text{(Sum of partial products)}.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n### Method 3: Distributive Property.\n\\[.\n(170 + 1)(270 + 1) = 170 \\times 270 + 170 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 270 + 1 \\times 1.\n\\].\n\\[.\n= 45,900 + 170 + 270 + 1 = 46,341.\n\\].\n\n### Method 4: Difference of Squares.\nRecognizing \\(171 = 221 - 50\\) and \\(271 = 221 + 50\\):.\n\\[.\n(221 - 50)(221 + 50) = 221^2 - 50^2.\n\\].\n\\[.\n221^2 = 48,841 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 50^2 = 2,500.\n\\].\n\\[. Therefore, the answer is"]] 53%|#####3    | 266/500 [1:31:28<22:33,  5.79s/it]
