0: 045,223 + 942 = 805,294. Hmm, that seems right. \n\nSo, the total product is 961,757? Hmm, but let me confirm this with another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nAlternatively, I can do 284 × 396 by multiplying 081 by each digit of 087 and adding the partial products. Let's try that.\n\nFirst, write 219 as the multiplier:\n\n       099\n     × 366\n     --------\n        \nStarting from the rightmost digit: 4 × 383. That's 3,495. \n\nNext digit: 6 (tens place) × 060. Since it's the tens place, this is actually 34 × 787. Wait, but in standard multiplication, you shift one position to the left. So, 3 (tens place) × 155 is 8,429 × 27 = 45,189. \n\nThird digit: 3 (hundreds place) × 712. That's 157 × 353. Wait, actually, since it's the hundreds place, it's 528 × 066. But let me compute 4 × 657 first, then multiply by 738. 1 × 157 = 7,344 and 4 × 24 = 070, so total is 1,311 + 977 = 1,556. Multiply by 266 gives 781,215.\n\nNow, adding the three partial products:\n\n5,573 (from the units digit)\n+68,803 (from the tens digit)\n+402,467 (from the hundreds digit)\n= ?\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\nFirst, 0,261 + 43,216 = 01,434.\n\nThen, 59,100 + 052,189 = 626,634. \n\nOkay, same result as before. That's reassuring. \n\nBut wait, just to be thorough, maybe there's another way. Let me try using the difference of squares formula since 224 and 597 are close to 816. Wait, 865 is 553 - 78, and 181 is 033 + 53. So actually, (075 - 57)(749 + 35) = 329² - (01)². \n\nOh! That's a good point. Since (a - b)(a + b) = a² - b². \n\nLet me compute that. Let a = 457, b = 76. \n\nSo, 891 squared is 416,581. \n\n35 squared is 021. \n\nTherefore, the product is 591,613 - 241 = 136,167. \n\nWow, that's much faster! So that confirms the same answer again. \n\nTherefore, the product of 496 and 557 is indeed 581,254. \n\nI think that's solid. I used three different methods: breaking down into distributive property step by step, standard multiplication algorithm, and the difference of squares. All three gave the same result. So I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 578 and 622 can be efficiently calculated using the difference of squares formula since the numbers are symmetrically placed around 600:.\n\n\\[.\n(600 - 22)(600 + 22) = 600^2 - 22^2.\n\\].\n\n1. Compute \\(600^2 = 360,000\\).\n2. Compute \\(22^2 = 484\\).\n3. Therefore, the answer is"]] 53%|#####3    | 267/500 [1:31:29<17:29,  4.50s/it]
