Break down 923 into 900 + 20 + 3:**.\n   \\[.\n   128 \\times 923 = 128 \\times (900 + 20 + 3).\n   \\].\n\n2. **Calculate each part separately:**.\n   - \\(128 \\times 900\\):.\n     \\[.\n     128 \\times 9 = 1152 \\quad \\text{so} \\quad 128 \\times 900 = 1152 \\times 100 = 115200.\n     \\].\n   - \\(128 \\times 20\\):.\n     \\[.\n     128 \\times 2 = 256 \\quad \\text{so} \\quad 128 \\times 20 = 256 \\times 10 = 2560.\n     \\].\n   - \\(128 \\times 3\\):.\n     \\[.\n     128 \\times 3 = 384.\n     \\].\n\n3. **Sum the results:**.\n   \\[.\n   115200 + 2560 + 384.\n   \\].\n   - First, add \\(115200 + 2560\\):.\n     \\[.\n     115200 + 2560 = 117760.\n     \\].\n   - Then add the result to 384:.\n     \\[.\n     117760 + 384 = 118144.\n     \\].\n\n4. **Verification using the standard multiplication algorithm:**.\n   - Multiply 128 by each digit of 923 (3, 20, 900) and sum the results:.\n     \\[.\n     \\begin{array}{r}.\n       \\quad 128 \\\\.\n     \\times 923 \\\\.\n     \\hline.\n       \\quad 384 \\quad (\\text{128 × 3}) \\\\.\n       2560 \\quad \\text{(128 × 20, shifted one position left)} \\\\.\n     +115200 \\quad \\text{(128 × 900, shifted two positions left)} \\\\.\n     \\hline.\n       118144 \\\\.\n     \\end{array}.\n     \\].\n\n5. **Cross-verification through division:**.\n   - Dividing the result by 128 gives 923:.\n     \\[.\n     118144 \\div 128 = 923.\n     \\].\n   - Dividing the result by 923 gives 128:.\n     \\[.\n     118144 \\div 923 = 128.\n     \\]. Therefore, the answer is"]] 57%|#####7    | 286/500 [1:32:19<07:46,  2.18s/it]
