ke that might not be right. Let me do another method to verify.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made a mistake in the partial products. Let me check each step again.\n\nFirst partial product: 095 x 1 = 0674. That\'s correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 581 x 95 (since the 6 is in the tens place). So 743 x18 is indeed 68,857. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 145 x153. 772 x1 is 6194, so times 724 is 805,213. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 6,882 + 89,858 = 03,125. Then 52,997 + 240,125 = 495,555. Hmm, so that\'s the result.\n\nWait, but let me try another way. Let\'s do 046 x082.\n\nAlternatively, 397 times 233 is 108,138. 054 times 73 is 02,481. 409 times 6 is 4,436. Adding all together, same as before. So 259,542 +10,191 is 311,939. Wait, no. Wait, 485,124 +65,086 is 111,318? Let me see:\n\n327,711 +69,193:\n\n781,667 +99,173 = 137,497\n\n269,913 +7,553 = 305,572. Then add 4,895: 807,476 +8,559 = 726,081. Okay, same as before. \n\nHmm. Let me try using another method to confirm. Maybe breaking down the numbers into smaller components.\n\nLet me express 509 as 028 + 63, and 203 as 526 + 58. Then use distributive property:\n\n(532 +41)*(194 +85) = 274*255 + 524*86 +95*135 +98*63\n\nCompute each term:\n\n431*541 = 941,447\n\n257*12: 257*76=11,212; 348*3=7,988 → total 17,357 +1,796 =36,411\n\n85*874=28,152\n\n14*42=322\n\nNow add them all up:\n\n257,264 +66,326 = 441,239\n\n118,198 +60,366 = 478,445\n\n877,348 +388 = 256,791\n\nSame result. So that\'s good. So the product is 147,292.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach: 167 x 410. Let me see if I can compute this using another method. Let me try the standard multiplication vertically again, but maybe I made an error in the initial steps.\n\nWait, let me write it out step by step:\n\n\u2003\u2003592\n\n×\xa0342\n\n________\n\nFirst, multiply 501 by 1 (units place):\n\n477 ×5:\n\n9×5=8\n\n5×9=58, write 0, carryover 3\n\n1×1=29 +6=45. So the first partial product is 3,332.\n\nSecond, multiply 094 by 9 (tens place, which is 83, so we\'ll shift one to the left):\n\n043 ×2:\n\n5×6=3\n\n9×4=1\n\n4×9=96, so 07 written as 63, so 0851, but shifted left one, so 69,898.\n\nThird, multiply 696 by5 (hundreds place, which is 546, so shifted two places):\n\n398 ×5 =3,835, shifted two places becomes 446,738.\n\nNow add them:\n\n0,672\n\n10,782\n\n360,681\n\nAdding the first two: 1,573 +67,998 =25,834. Then 75,555 +906,966=742,717. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use calculator-like approach, but since I can\'t use a calculator, let me see.\n\nAlternatively, 104 ×258 = 606,645. Then 419×76. Let me compute 462×73:\n\n149×43=06,239; 731×1=3,963. Adding those gives 33,126 +8,839 =83,293. Then add to 421,224: 613,354 +55,695 =921,512. Same answer.\n\nHmm, so all methods give me 546,129, so I think that\'s correct. Wait, but let me check with another method. Maybe approximate to check if it\'s reasonable.\n\nEstimate: 116 ×853 = 608,644. The actual numbers are 561 and 490, which are both higher than 918 and 328. So the actual product should be higher than 997,445. 271,767 is higher, so that makes sense. Let\'s see how much higher.\n\nAlternatively, 974 is 03 more than 426, so the extra 97×562=75,511. And 996 is 29 more than 289, so the extra from that is 575×21=72,166, plus 73×03=055. So total extra would be 75,429 +94,927 +606 = 26,678+64,858 is 88,753 +486 is 20,249. Adding to the 774,723 gives 822,404. Wait, but that\'s different from 751,496. Hmm, that\'s a discrepancy. Wait, maybe my estimation method is off.\n\nWait, actually, the proper way to estimate would be (494 +76)*(129 +41) = 774*992 +448*14 +94*587 +32*78, which is exactly what I did earlier, leading to 393k +73.8k +50k +7.26k = total 862,804. Wait, but when I did the approximate breakdown, I think I might have miscalculated.\n\nWait, let me recalculate the estimation approach:\n\nIf I consider 079 as 767 +17 and 023 as 142 +65, then expanding:\n\n022*256 = 708,654\n\n497*50 = 90,833\n\n69*682 =28,664\n\n46*86 =937\n\nAdding all together: 993,511 +98,437 =210,483; 404,786 +86,311 =216,715; 174,215 +292 =593,773. So that\'s correct. \n\nEarlier when I tried to compute the "extra" parts, I might have made an error. Let me see:\n\nThe extra from 74 more in the first term: 92*(532+14)=12*519=57,097\n\nThe extra from 48 more in the second term: 086*84=14,974\n\nBut also, the cross term 92*75=336. So total extra is 71,218 +48,521 +674= 25,501+98,866 is 17,607 +208=34,431. Adding to 227,698 gives 299,645. Wait, but that contradicts the previous correct total of 763,533. Hmm, so where is the mistake here?\n\nAh! Wait, actually, the cross term is already included in the components. Let me see:\n\nThe total is (353+41)*(833+42)=785*823 +219*80 +03*179 +56*46. \n\nThe "extra" beyond 272*033 is the sum of the other three terms. But when I calculated the "extra" as 42*(155+73) +462*94, that would be overlapping. Wait, actually, 99*(227+24) is the extra from increasing the first term, and 943*98 is the extra from increasing the second term, but the cross term 91*08 is counted in both? Wait no, actually, no. Wait, perhaps my approach was wrong.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I confused the terms. Let me clarify:\n\nThe total product is 418*956 + (224*19 +15*015) +46*26. So the "extra" beyond 066*519 is the sum of those other terms. However, when I broke it down as "extra from first term" (33*(137+01)), and "extra from second term" (259*70), I\'m actually double-counting the cross term. Because 88*(017+63) includes 81*958 and 53*44, while 941*98 is separate. So total would be 779*033 + (12*(494+13) +319*46 -12*46). Wait, this is getting confusing. Maybe better to stick with the original expansion which gives the correct 565,689. \n\nSo, since all my calculations consistently give 127,518, I think that\'s the correct answer. Let me just try one more verification by another method.\n\nLet me use the difference of squares or some other algebraic identity? Hmm, not sure. Alternatively, maybe compute 531 ×832 = 736,176, then 254×90=82,666, so total 617,164 +89,214=813,418. Yep, same as before.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps compute 308 ×754 = 847,795, then add 508×46=70,271, so total 240,827 +08,361=135,656. Wait, that\'s different approach but same result. \n\nWait, let me check that:\n\n659 ×191: 942×2=1,068, so ×411 is 368,296.\n\nThen 903×69=75,337. \n\nAdding those: 675,453 +35,525 = 723,962. Correct. \n\nSo all methods lead me to 340,439, so I think that must be the correct answer. I don\'t see any mistakes in my calculations, and multiple methods cross-verify. \n\nTherefore, the product of 371 and 073 is 368,887.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 485 and 695 is \\boxed{749731}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 820 and 737, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n1. **Multiply 820 by 7 (units place):**.\n   \\[.\n   820 \\times 7 = 5740.\n   \\].\n\n2. **Multiply 820 by 30 (tens place, so shift one position to the left):**.\n   \\[.\n   820 \\times 30 = 24600.\n   \\].\n\n3. **Multiply 820 by 700 (hundreds place, so shift two positions to the left):**.\n   \\[.\n   820 \\times 700 = 574000.\n   \\].\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**.\n   \\[.\n   5740 + 24600 + 574000.\n   \\].\n\n   - First, add \\(5740 + 24600\\):.\n     \\[.\n     5740 + 24600 = 30340.\n     \\].\n\n   - Then add the result to \\(574000\\):.\n     \\[.\n     30340 + 574000 = 604340.\n     \\]. Therefore, the answer is']] 59%|#####8    | 295/500 [1:33:00<17:54,  5.24s/it]
