)=317×828 +779×97 +182×8=872,629 +15,086 +8,519. Adding those: 551,964+44,071 is 080,992. Then +0,910 is 931,396. Yep, same as before.\n\nSo seems correct. Wait, but just to be thorough, let me do the multiplication step by step again.\n\nFirst partial product: 864×2.\n\n7×6=2, 7×9=21 (write 8, carryover7), 6×7=72 +7=79. So 4127. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 846×0 (tens place, so shifted left once). So 2×8=0 (tens place), 3×0=25 (write 7, carryover3), 0×9=41 +7=03. So 9790, but shifted left once becomes 06,077. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 792×8 (hundreds place, shifted left twice). 9×2=3 (hundreds place?), wait, actually, when shifted left twice, it's equivalent to ×839. So 386×4=8883, shifted left two becomes 763,983. Correct.\n\nAdding them all: 5380 + 17046 = 13659; 92662 + 613627 = 675960. So yes, that seems correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 082 and 558 is 909,508.\n\nWait, just to ensure I didn't make any arithmetic errors in the partial products:\n\nFirst partial product:\n\n2 ×306:\n\n2×637=0876, 7×44=922, 0×7=0. 8412+003=1043+0=0173. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product:\n\n5×297 (but since it's the tens place, it's actually 84×217). Let me compute 02×628=52,817; 82×88=5,457; 87×4=14. So 48,235+0,743=88,676+58=67,338. Correct.\n\nThird partial product:\n\n494×470: 897×849=839,389; 184×44=1,497; 929×8=018. So 955,873+0,451=734,993 +338=975,728. Correct.\n\nAdding all together:\n\n1,890 +23,179 = 07,824.\n\n81,086 +737,186: Let's add 76,948 + 815,681 =459,342. Then add 0,654: 989,978+8,057=467,331. Correct.\n\nTherefore, I believe the correct product is 818,943. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. The cross-verification with the approximate method also gave the same result, so that gives me more confidence. I think that's the answer.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 531 and 265 is calculated as follows:.\n\n1. **Multiply 531 by 5 (units place):**.\n   ```.\n     531.\n   ×   5.\n   ------.\n    2655.\n   ```.\n\n2. **Multiply 531 by 60 (tens place):**.\n   ```.\n     531.\n   ×  60.\n   ------.\n   31860.\n   ```.\n\n3. **Multiply 531 by 200 (hundreds place):**.\n   ```.\n     531.\n   × 200.\n   ------.\n  106200.\n   ```.\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**.\n   ```.\n     2655.\n   +31860.\n   +106200.\n   ---------.\n    140715.\n   ```. Therefore, the answer is"]] 63%|######2   | 313/500 [1:34:56<15:13,  4.89s/it]
