final_output:  ['\\boxed{90914}.\n\nWait, the user asked for the product of 347 and 262, but in the thought process above, there were some inconsistencies and miscalculations. Let me correct that step-by-step properly.\n\n### Correct Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nTo find the product of 347 and 262:\n\n1. **Multiply 347 by 2 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   347 \\times 2 = 694\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 347 by 60 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   347 \\times 60 = 347 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 2082 \\times 10 = 20820\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 347 by 200 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   347 \\times 200 = 347 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 694 \\times 100 = 69400\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the results of the three multiplications:**\n   \\[\n   694 + 20820 + 69400\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(694\\) and \\(20820\\):\n     \\[\n     694 + 20820 = 21514\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to \\(69400\\):\n     \\[\n     21514 + 69400 = 90914\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 347 and 262 is \\(\\boxed{90914}\\).', '']
