     149 \\times 8 = 1,192 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 1,192 \\times 100 = 119,200.\n     \\].\n   - **149 × 30:**.\n     \\[.\n     149 \\times 3 = 447 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 447 \\times 10 = 4,470.\n     \\].\n   - **149 × 1:**.\n     \\[.\n     149 \\times 1 = 149.\n     \\].\n\n3. **Sum the results of each multiplication:**.\n   \\[.\n   119,200 + 4,470 + 149 = 123,819.\n   \\].\n\n**Verification with Alternative Methods:**.\n- **Using nearby numbers:**  .\n  \\(150 \\times 831 = 124,650\\)  .\n  Subtract \\(1 \\times 831\\) (since \\(150 - 1 = 149\\)):  .\n  \\(124,650 - 831 = 123,819\\).\n\n- **Distributive property (breaking down both numbers):**  .\n  \\[.\n  (100 + 40 + 9) \\times (800 + 30 + 1) = 83,100 + 33,240 + 7,479 = 123,819.\n  \\].\n\n**Final Answer:**. Therefore, the answer is"]] 66%|######6   | 330/500 [1:35:24<05:56,  2.10s/it]
