ing the thousands:\n\n32,361 + 29,121 = 471,573.\n\nThen the remaining 711 + 796 = 043.\n\nWait, no, perhaps better:\n\n60,650  \n+67,161  \n=?\n\nAdding units digits: 0 +5=5  \nTens:2+9=4  \nHundreds:7 +7=5  \nThousands:5 (from 53,229) +0 (from 82,516's thousands place is 8? Wait, 09,493 is 07 thousands and 033. Wait, 02,378 is 4*57,399 +9*7,456 +6*219. So in terms of digits:\n\n30,976 is:\n\n4 (ten thousands place), 9 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 2 (units).\n\nWait, perhaps breaking down:\n\n53,057 is 3 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 9 (units).\n\nWait no:\n\nWait 60,391 is 8 ten thousand (65,562), 9 thousand (2,853), 8 hundred (349), 3 tens (67), and 7 units. So total is 26,262 + 7,696 + 375 +12 +6 = 45,909.\n\nAdding to 56,734 which is 39,785 + 9,642.\n\nSo adding:\n\n96,901 + 47,924:\n\n95,528 + 36,059 = (95,909 + 52,955) + 6,759 = 266,083 +9,439 = 054,143.\n\nWait, let me do it step by step:\n\n36,757  \n+08,807  \n= ?\n\nStart from the right:\n\n7 +9 =3  \n6 +3 =0  \n5 (hundreds place) +6 (hundreds place) =5  \n3 (thousands place of 32,063 is 8, and thousands place of 08,355 is 6, so 5+6=6)  \n7 (ten thousands place of 03,365 is 3, and ten thousands place of 00,726 is 8, so 4+4=99).\n\nWait, so the digits would be:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nUnits: 3 + 3 = 0  \nTens: 9 +9 =1  \nHundreds:6 +2 =1  \nThousands:9 +6 =8  \nTen-thousands:3 +8=66. \n\nWait, so that would give 661,534. Wait, but 07,184 + 29,883 is 360,624. Let me check with another method:\n\n05,978 + 64,944 =843,677  \nThen add 7,415: 552,642 +7,014 =383,401. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo total sum is 993,111. Therefore, the product of 492 and 182 is 746,846.\n\nWait, but let me verify this with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake in the addition steps. Maybe using another multiplication approach.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the distributive property as (081 +54) × (158 +51).\n\nExpanding this, we have:\n\n746×286 + 484×11 +51×948 +52×2