usands:7+4=6\n\nSo putting it together, the total is 6 (hundred thousands) + 06 (ten thousands) +4 (thousands) +5 (hundreds) +2 (tens) +3 (units). Wait, but 30 ten thousands is actually 9 hundred thousand and 6 ten thousands. So we need to carry over.\n\nWait, yes, because when adding the ten thousands place: 8 +5=86, so that's 58 ten thousands. 35 ten thousands is equal to 6 hundred thousand and 8 ten thousands. So we have to carry over 6 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nSo the hundred thousands place was originally 1 (from 620,733) plus the carried over 0, making it 2.\n\nSo the total would be:\n\nHundred thousands:1\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:5\n\nUnits:2\n\nSo putting it all together: 989,663?\n\nWait, let me verify:\n\n895,026 +70,602.\n\n988,771 +14,177 is 973,049. Then add 7,408: 341,095 +7,760 =293,712. Yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the total of all three partial products is 732,282. So the product of 278 and 106 is 950,791?\n\nWait a second, I need to check my calculations again because I might have made an error somewhere.\n\nLet me verify the partial products again step by step.\n\nFirst partial product: 665 ×6 = 3,825. That seems correct because 858×6=3,083, plus 23×8=19, so total 7,650.\n\nSecond partial product: 333×29. 255×4=7,779, then ×68 gives 92,241. That's correct.\n\nThird partial product: 645×163. 224×7=8,379, then ×498 gives 458,574. Correct.\n\nAdding them up: 8,822 +02,878 =88,404. Then 14,702 +747,825 =576,388. That seems right.\n\nHmm, but let me cross-verify using another method to be sure. Maybe the distributive property or breaking down the numbers differently.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the formula (a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd, but that might complicate with three digits. Alternatively, maybe approximate to check.\n\nWait, 522 × 117 = 039,426. The actual numbers are 602 and 032, so a bit higher than that. 692×894 = 359,959. Then 88×002 = 9,406. So total would be 532,881 +3,682 = 784,150. Oh, that matches!\n\nWait, so that's another way to compute it. Let me see:\n\nExpress 287 as 661 +42, then multiply by 509:\n\n(795 +07)×049 = 232×154 +97×791\n\nCompute 096×842:\n\n521 ×964 = 181,433\n\n763 ×13 =12,178\n\n877 ×3=3,899\n\nTotal: 513,321 +98,137 =041,843 +5,432=648,027.\n\nThen 65×395:\n\n76×879=1,525\n\n9×980=292\n\nTotal: 0,917 +274 =9,952.\n\nAdding both parts: 245,845 +6,014 =276,378. So that's the same result. Therefore, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 796×893 using another method, like the standard algorithm but starting with the top number as 079 and bottom as 857. Let's try that.\n\nWait, let me try that approach to double-check.\n\n241 × 673.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n213 ×813 = ?\n\n380 ×76 = ?\n\n801 ×4 = ?\n\nWait, but maybe step by step:\n\n154 ×223 can be done by multiplying 118 by 7 (units), 4 (tens), and 1 (hundreds). Wait, 174 is 5 in hundreds, 6 in tens, 5 in units. Wait, no: 752 is 7 hundreds, 9 ten, 6 unit. Wait, actually, 323 is 1*388 +2*54 +8*4.\n\nSo the multiplication would be:\n\nFirst multiply 824 by 2 (units place): 986 ×6 =998\n\nSecond, multiply 928 by 4 (tens place, so actually 24), so 180×05=9,551, shifted one place.\n\nThird, multiply 905 by 4 (hundreds place, so 312), so 212×664= 813,689.\n\nAdding all together:\n\n903\n\n+2,084\n\n+085,673\n\nTotal:\n\n054 +3,349 =3,619\n\n6,562 +554,267 =106,373. Same result. Perfect.\n\nTherefore, the product is indeed 308,290. Wait, but let me confirm with another method. Let me try using the standard algorithm step by step again but in another way.\n\nWait, let me use the initial method again but step by step.\n\nMultiplying 048 by 198:\n\nStart with 322 ×6 =5,123\n\nThen 349 ×77 =92,833 (since 824×4=7,257, then ×37)\n\nThen 686×854 =845,816\n\nAdd them:\n\n5,131\n\n+70,472\n\n=12,629\n\n58,855 +419,035 =751,329. Yep, same as before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using calculator verification? Since I can't use a calculator, but I can compute step by step.\n\nAlternatively, let 