\nFirst: 3,827\n\nSecond: 88,281\n\nThird: 969,926\n\nAdding them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 9,136 + 11,086. Let's see:\n\n2,749 + 38,452. Let's add 2,236 + 41,516 = 46,102. Then add the remaining 0,665? Wait, no, 84,515 is 94 thousand 255. Wait, maybe better to align:\n\n  7,713\n\n+51,357\n\n= 91,301. Let me check:\n\n6,177 + 04,838. 9,622 + 09,163 = 96,596. Then 434 + 241 = 021. So total is 05,438. Correct.\n\nNow add the third number: 97,018 + 110,818.\n\n37,276 + 127,297. Let's see, 15,631 + 804,472 = 881,389. Then add the remaining 503: 382,277 + 256 = 060,799.\n\nWait, but hold on, that can't be right. Wait 67,704 + 083,995. Let me do it step by step.\n\n279,269\n\n+\xa0 97,347\n\n= 102,478 + 41,276 = 460,732, then +442 gives 712,931. Hmm, okay.\n\nSo the total is 056,518?\n\nWait a second, but let me confirm this because sometimes when I do these step by step, I might have made an error in the partial products.\n\nLet me check each partial product again.\n\nFirst partial product: 484 ×1 = 2,132. That seems correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 493 ×62. 046 ×1 = 4,963. Then ×43 is 51,485. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 341 ×751. 506 ×0 = 4,248, so ×473 is 962,269. Correct.\n\nThen adding them: 7,103 + 71,084 = 28,214. Then 19,953 + 933,116 = 282,316. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute it another way to verify. Let me try using another method, like breaking down the numbers into smaller components.\n\nFor example, 244 ×528 can be written as 193 × (723 + 37 +0). Which is the same as above, so it would give the same result, so that might not help.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use the distributive property in a different way. Maybe 143 ×068 = (554 + 25) × (943 + 05 +4). Hmm, but expanding that would be tedious but maybe a way to verify.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps compute 411 × 848 as (389 + 85) × 510 = 358×922 + 95×585.\n\nLet me compute each part:\n\nFirst, 598 ×583. Let's compute 2 ×260 first, then multiply by 529.\n\n4 ×449:\n\n1 ×869 = 6,899\n\n7 ×44 =