two positions left:**.\n   \\[.\n   508 \\times 400 = 203200.\n   \\].\n   - \\(508 \\times 4 = 2032\\), then add two zeros.\n\n**Adding the partial products:**.\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n     3556 \\\\.\n   + 20320 \\\\.\n + 203200 \\\\.\n \\hline.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n- Adding \\(3556 + 20320 = 23876\\).\n- Adding \\(23876 + 203200 = 227076\\).\n\n**Verification using Distributive Property:**.\n\\[.\n508 \\times 447 = (500 + 8)(400 + 40 + 7).\n\\].\nExpanding and summing each term:.\n\\[.\n\\begin{aligned}.\n&500 \\times 400 = 200000, \\\\.\n&500 \\times 40 = 20000, \\\\.\n&500 \\times 7 = 3500, \\\\.\n&8 \\times 400 = 3200, \\\\.\n&8 \\times 40 = 320, \\\\.\n&8 \\times 7 = 56.\n\\end{aligned}.\n\\].\nSumming these:.\n\\[. Therefore, the answer is"]] 72%|#######2  | 362/500 [1:36:56<04:09,  1.81s/it]
