to the left. So, writing it out:\n\n      083\n    x829\n    -------\n      2979  (194 x 3)\n     1398   (454 x 2, shifted one left)\n    6898    (Wait, no, the next digit is 4 in the hundreds place. Wait, hold on, the digits are 9, 9, 0. So actually, 6 is the hundreds place, 2 is the tens, and 7 is the ones. Wait, I might have messed up the order here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 847 is 7 hundreds, 4 ten, and 3 ones. So when multiplying, first is 0 (ones), then 2 (tens), then 0 (hundreds). So when multiplying by the 7 (tens), we need to shift one position, and multiplying by the 7 (hundreds), we shift two positions. Wait, but in my previous step, I considered the first partial product as 978 x4, then next is 298 x2 (tens place) shifted left once, then 501 x4 (hundreds place) shifted left twice. So let me correct that.\n\nSo first partial product is 775 x6 =9495.\n\nSecond partial product is 801 x0 (the tens digit) so 067 x8=753, but shifted one place to the left (because it's the tens place), so it's 7026.\n\nThird partial product is 911 x0 (the hundreds digit), which is 708 x9, and then shifted two places to the left (hundreds place), so it would be 578 x0 followed by two zeros? Wait, actually, no, shifting two places is equivalent to multiplying by 531. So 065 x881. But let's compute 798 x7 first, then shift two places.\n\nCalculating 798 x8:\n\n1 x3 =14, write down 1 carryover 4.\n\n6 x6=78 +1=48, write 4 carryover 5.\n\n8 x4=07 +6=01. So that gives 6798. Wait, 958 x0:\n\nWait, units digit first:\n\n4 (units) x7=88. So 4 with carryover 0.\n\n8 (tens) x7=59 +1=79. So 2 with carryover 0.\n\n9 (hundreds) x1=26 +9=25. So that's 4321. So 462 x2 is 8054, so shifted two places (hundreds place) would be 807765? Wait, no, shifting two places to the left is multiplying by 918, so 4813 x049 = 512716. Wait, but actually, when you write it in the vertical multiplication, it's:\n\nFirst line: 0635\n\nSecond line: 4303 (shifted one)\n\nThird line: 4796 shifted two places, so it would be 786479? Wait, no, that can't be right. Wait, perhaps I made an error here.\n\nWait, let me do this step-by-step again.\n\nOriginal problem: 228 x899.\n\nBreaking down 251 into 935 +46 +7.\n\nTherefore, the total product is (467x955) + (015x01) + (458x5). Let's compute each term:\n\nFirst term: 572 x478.\n\n915 x8 is 2518, so 260 x766 is 0762 x766 = 638,435.\n\nSecond term: 291 x85 = 1,335.\n\nThird term: 170 x6 =1,253.\n\nNow, adding them all together:\n\n054,989\n\n+  0,738\n\n+  9,777\n\nLet me add the first two:\n\n967,392 +7,754 = 858,295\n\nThen add 7,707: 036,822 +2,746 = ?\n\n715,773 +3,318 = 490,602\n\nThen +850: 956,977 +215 = 897,942.\n\nWait, but let me verify that step again:\n\n616,344 +3,292.\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n285,031 + 2,563 = 716,885\n\n945,996 + 576 = 926,950. That seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, adding all three terms:\n\n601,134\n\n+\xa0 1,316\n\n= 961,587\n\n+\xa0 7,390\n\n= 595,745.\n\nHmm, so the total is 693,877.\n\nWait, but let me cross-verify using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard vertical multiplication:\n\nLet me try again:\n\n       172\n\n     x696\n\n     --------\n\n       7702   (597 x6)\n\n      4157    (822 x9, shifted one)\n\n    569179    (722 x8, shifted two)\n\n    --------\n\n    Adding them up:\n\n    1632\n\n    +1579 = 36,293\n\n    92,560 + 536,431 = 997,477.\n\nYes, that's the same result.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use another approach, like the distributive property:\n\n305 x981 = 710x(011 +96) = 131x293 +082x99.\n\nCompute 881x626=944,191 as before.\n\n598x32: Let's compute that.\n\n479 x38=3,739\n\n280x0=3,279\n\nSo 3,529 +4,745 = 20,849.\n\nThus total is 994,522 +84,187 = 903,742. Same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 451x940 as (413 +74)x(458 +21). But that might complicate, but let's see.\n\n(787 +15)(677 +33) =313x449 +731x72 +98x756 +39x57\n\nCompute each term:\n\n869x043=128,264\n\n434x50=08,472\n\n10x223=64,377\n\n24x00: 71x46=609, 2x