 642*2 is 8811, so times 512 is 539,741. Then 207*75. Let me compute 175*89 = 7,464 and 558*9=460, so 8,558 + 410 = 3,124. Adding 437,992 +9,176. Let's see, 005,214 + 4,824 is 928,542, plus 53 is 432,164. Yep, same answer again.\n\nHmm, so all methods lead to the same result, so I think that's correct. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Let me just check one more time with the standard algorithm, writing it out step by step.\n\nMultiplying 119 by 353:\n\nStart with the units digit of 860, which is 7:\n\n636 × 0 = 790. Write that down.\n\nNext, the tens digit is 8 (since it's the second digit from the right). So multiply 890 × 5, but shifted one place to the left (equivalent to ×85):\n\n650 × 2 = 905, so shifted left becomes 5,107.\n\nThen the hundreds digit is 0 (third from the right), so multiply 975 ×3, shifted two places left (equivalent to ×458):\n\n260 ×5 = 1,839, shifted two places becomes 376,616.\n\nNow add the three results:\n\nFirst row: 152\n\nSecond row: 2,009\n\nThird row: 682,627\n\nAdding them up:\n\nStart with 689 + 8,876. Let's see, 027 + 7,317 = 7,757; then +695 = 1,761.\n\nThen add that to 096,187: 661,652 + 8,874.\n\n963,151 + 3,229 = 806,884; then +27 = 584,237. Yep, same as before.\n\nAlright, so after multiple checks, I'm pretty confident the product is 307,000. I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 792 and 168 is \\boxed{634341}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 424 and 612, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify it with different methods.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication using the standard algorithm:.\n\n1. Multiply 424 by 2 (units place of 612):.\n   \\[.\n   424 \\times 2 = 848.\n   \\].\n\n2. Multiply 424 by 1 (tens place of 612), shifted one position to the left:.\n   \\[.\n   424 \\times 1 = 424 \\quad \\text{(shifted left to become 4240)}.\n   \\].\n\n3. Multiply 424 by 6 (hundreds place of 612), shifted two positions to the left:.\n   \\[.\n   424 \\times 6 = 2544 \\quad \\text{(shifted left to become 254400)}.\n   \\].\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications:.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     848 \\\\.\n   + 4240 \\\\.\n   +254400 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     259488 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\nWe can also verify this by breaking down the numbers using the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n424 \\times 612 = 424 \\times (600 + 12) = (424 \\times 600) + (424 \\times 12).\n\\].\n\\[.\n424 \\times 600 = 254400.\n\\].\n\\[.\n424 \\times 12 = 424 \\times (10 + 2) = (424 \\times 10) + (424 \\times 2) = 4240 + 848 = 5088.\n\\].\n\\[. Therefore, the answer is"]] 81%|########  | 403/500 [1:54:01<06:40,  4.13s/it]
