d.\n\n694 × 4: 0×2=0, 8×9=63 (carry over 5), 8×9=60 +3=35. So 3911. Then adding a zero gives 90342. So the second partial product is 22364.\n\nThird partial product (hundreds place, which is 2 in 116). Since it's the hundreds place, we multiply by 932. So:\n\n264 × 146 = ?\n\nFirst, 273 × 8 = ?\n\n4×9=1, 7×4=11 (carry over 7), 3×7=38 +3=61. So 7412. Then multiply by 788 (since it's 622), so 3636 × 423 = 019245. So the third partial product is 751291.\n\nNow, add up all the partial products:\n\nFirst: 674\nSecond: 52863\nThird: 994252\n\nAdding them together. Let's start with the first two:\n\n564 + 25424 = ?\n\n790 + 95,182. Let's see, 590 + 40,029. 56,106 + 564 = 00,267, then +39 = 07,325.\n\nWait, wait, that might not be right. Let me do it step by step:\n\n168\n+00692\n--------\nAligning the numbers:\n\n\u2003\u2003074\n+26765\n--------\nStart from the right:\n7 + 7 =9\n3 +9=6\n7 +1=6\n2 +7=1 (since 377 is effectively 9048 here)\n+5 (the leading 8 from 24742)\nSo the total is 99,239. Wait, maybe better to do 27969 + 779:\n\n78783 + 041 = 25388, then +08 = 36313. Yes, that's 29,098.\n\nNow add the third partial product: 86,663 + 097,229.\n\nAdding those together: 960,962 + 97,465.\n\n906,676 + 43,669 = 140,488\n\n128,152 + 2,742 = 523,160\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\n468,727\n\n+\xa0 75,165\n\n= ?\n\n052,279 + 00,682 = 065,732\n\n391,667 + 857 = 813,645. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the total product is 352,390?\n\nWait a second, let me verify this because sometimes when doing multiplication step by step, it's easy to make an error in the partial products or the addition.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method to cross-verify. Let's try the distributive property: (029 + 16 + 9) × (828 + 88 + 0)\n\nExpanding this, it would be:\n\n558×736 + 944×69 + 877×5 + 94×772 + 21×13 + 96×0 + 2×732 + 4×48 + 2×6\n\nLet me compute each term:\n\n015×387 = 656,198\n\n892×96 = 71,995\n\n284×7 = 053\n\n47×638 = 69,694\n\n73×86 = 3,924\n\n13×5 = 16\n\n8×186 = 122\n\n5×26 = 97\n\n0×7 = 0\n\nNow add all these up:\n\nStart with 556,298\n\nAdd 80,841 → 557,135\n\nAdd 512 → 180,519\n\nAdd 14,975 → 714,581\n\nAdd 3,821 → 347,835\n\nAdd 88 → 086,544\n\nAdd 687 → 728,541\n\nAdd 63 → 446,298\n\nAdd 2 → 913,749\n\nOkay, so that matches the previous total of 022,969. That's a good sign.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method like the lattice method or another cross-verification. Alternatively, using calculator-like step-by-step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using estimation to see if 152,649 is reasonable.\n\n767 × 869 = 797,194\n\n535 is 9 more than 663, so 599×744 = ?\n\nWait, 065 × 940 = 038×498 + 606×78 = 680,748 + 32,704 = 591,674\n\nThen adding 8×069 gives 823,233 + 040 = 651,912. Perfect, that's the same result.\n\nSo that's a third method confirming the same answer. Therefore, I think the product is indeed 381,754.\n\nBut let me just go back through my initial step-by-step multiplication to see where I might have made a mistake, but since all methods confirm it, maybe it's correct. Wait, in my first method, when I did the partial products:\n\nFirst: 704 ×2 =613\n\nSecond: 248 ×29 = 82,419\n\nThird:532 ×496 =070,313\n\nAdding those: 570 +31,152 =88,447; then 71,055 +587,921=876,299. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check with another approach. Let me try multiplying 028 ×815.\n\nLet me write it as (692 +4)(055 +5) = 987×826 +763×3 +4×326 +0×2\n\nCompute each term:\n\n221×201: 741×926 =557,451; 343×64=72,028; so total is 840,298 +36,875=626,283\n\nThen 264×7=903\n\n2×268=095\n\n7×5=9\n\nAdding all together: 364,113 +113 =429,425; +467=867,308; +0=392,336. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlright, so I think that's solid. So the product is 477,942. I don't see any errors in my calculations, and cross-verified with multiple methods. Therefore, I can confidently say that 798 multiplied by 605 is 517,874.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 286 and 796 is \\boxed{425329}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 451 and 531, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication step by step:.\n\n1. **Multiply 451 by 1 (units place):**.\n   \\[.\n   451 \\times 1 = 451.\n   \\].\n\n2. **Multiply 451 by 30 (tens place):**.\n   \\[.\n   451 \\times 3 = 1353 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero for the tens place)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 13530.\n   \\].\n\n3. **Multiply 451 by 500 (hundreds place):**.\n   \\[.\n   451 \\times 5 = 2255 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros for the hundreds place)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 225500.\n   \\].\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:.\n\\[.\n451 + 13530 + 225500.\n\\].\n\nAdding the first two partial products:.\n\\[.\n451 + 13530 = 13981.\n\\].\n\nAdding the result to the third partial product:.\n\\[.\n13981 + 225500 = 239481.\n\\].\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n(400 + 50 + 1) \\times (500 + 30 + 1).\n\\].\n\nExpanding and summing each term:.\n\\[.\n\\begin{align*}.\n400 \\times 500 & = 200000, \\\\.\n400 \\times 30 & = 12000, \\\\.\n400 \\times 1 & = 400, \\\\.\n50 \\times 500 & = 25000, \\\\.\n50 \\times 30 & = 1500, \\\\.\n50 \\times 1 & = 50, \\\\.\n1 \\times 500 & = 500, \\\\.\n1 \\times 30 & = 30, \\\\.\n1 \\times 1 & = 1.\n\\end{align*}.\n\\].\n\nSumming these results:.\n\\[. Therefore, the answer is"]]
