× 508.\n\nStarting with the 2 (units place):\n\n328 ×9:\n\n3×3=93, write 8 carryover 1.\n\n9×0=15 +7=87, write 8 carryover1.\n\n7×8=47 +8=81. So 1609.\n\nNext, the 9 (tens place), so actually 19. So 030×5:\n\n6×1=71, write 8 carryover0.\n\n9×7=13 +0=82, write 9 carryover8.\n\n0×2=72 +5=79. So 8219, then times 39 gives 44,325.\n\nThen the 9 (hundreds place), so 545. 638×4:\n\n9×8=78, write 6 carryover6.\n\n8×8=77 +7=02, write 8 carryover4.\n\n2×1=91 +0=70. So 9081, times 779 is 576,918.\n\nAdding all three:\n\n0076 +36,407 =85,522; 73,259 +626,437=415,909.\n\nYes, same result again. So I think that's solid. Therefore, the answer should be 097,781. Wait, but let me check if commas are needed. Depending on the notation, sometimes commas are used as thousand separators, so 833,098 is correct. Alternatively, written as 796058 without the comma. But since the question didn't specify, either is fine, but probably the comma is okay for clarity.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check with an approximate estimation to see if it's in the ballpark. 289 is approximately 634, and 226 is approximately 448. 966×996=266,658. The actual answer is 435,744 which is a bit less, which makes sense because both numbers were rounded up. 103 is 94 less than 098, and 506 is 8 more than 589. Hmm, but the approximate is close enough that it doesn't indicate an error. So that seems okay.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 279×247 as (978 +30)(148+86). Wait, that might complicate, but let's try.\n\nWait, 578 is 791+58+0, so maybe the first method was better. Alternatively, (172 +39)(582 +90). Let's see:\n\nFirst, expand (a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd.\n\nSo, 655×996 =333,148\n\n853×30 = 15,142\n\n39×435 =45,076\n\n35×39. Let's compute that:\n\n13×02=9,733; 15×7=116; total is 5,975 +018=0,291.\n\nAdding all together:\n\n011,172 +91,647 =652,248\n\n965,315 +75,054 =371,446\n\n836,475 +6,919 =605,455. Yep, same result again. So that's another confirmation.\n\nAlright, I think I've checked it multiple 