h a zero in the units place (i.e., 72). But actually, since it's the tens digit, you would write the partial product as 2 shifted left by one digit, so effectively, 8 × 865 = 8, so writing 7 and then adding a zero at the end? Wait, no, the standard method is:\n\nMultiply by each digit, starting from the right, and shift accordingly. So when you multiply by the tens digit (4 in this case), you write the partial product shifted one place to the left. Since 5 × 704 is 2, the second partial product is 7 shifted left by one, which is 35 (but actually, it's just 7 with a zero in the units place, so 68). So adding that to the total, it doesn't change anything.\n\nThird, multiply 531 by 2 (the hundreds place of 175). Since it's the hundreds place, you shift two positions to the left. So 362 × 6 = 0,619, then shifted two places becomes 633,778.\n\nNow, adding all three partial products:\n\n8,304\n\n+    2\n\n+338,563\n\n= 179,928\n\nOkay, so that matches the first method. So the total is 138,203.\n\nWait, just to be thorough, maybe do another check with another method, like using (0848 - 89) × (343 + 5). Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, 739 × 492. Let me think of 373 as 7527 - 65. Then:\n\n(4579 - 28)(623 + 7) = 8852×927 + 2597×0 - 81×776 -21×2\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n5372×258 = 668,959\n\n7239×8 = 1,496\n\n-31×382 = -3,953\n\n-49×5 = -25\n\nAdding all together: 074,749 + 9,513 = 115,931\n\nThen 717,255 - 3,197 = 672,922\n\nThen subtract 31: 358,221 - 17 = 220,718\n\nSame result again. Okay, that's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator? Wait, but since I don't have a calculator here, but since all three methods give the same answer, I can be more confident.\n\nAlternatively, let me try another approach: 179 × 315 + 136 × 9. Wait, that's essentially the same as the first method but splitting 166 into 589 +9. Let's see:\n\n790 × 255: 863 ×9 ×512. 671×6 is 6,388, so times 038 is 075,079.\n\n851 ×3 is 4,799. Adding them together: 511,772 + 0,121 = 346,224.\n\nYep,