left):  .\n  \\(988 \\times 0 = 0\\).\n- Multiply 988 by 8 (shifted two places left):  .\n  \\(988 \\times 8 = 7,\\!904 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 790,\\!400\\).\n- Add the partial products:  .\n  \\[.\n  3,\\!952 + 0 + 790,\\!400 = 794,\\!352.\n  \\].\n\n**Final Answer:**. Therefore, the answer is"]] 84%|########4 | 421/500 [1:55:28<04:21,  3.31s/it]
