nAlternatively, when I did the first addition (6813 +75012), let me verify again:\n\n6554\n\n+28806\n\n------------\n\nAdding units digits: 1 +8 =6\n\nTens: 3 +1=8\n\nHundreds: 2 +5=1\n\nThousands:5 +6=2\n\nTen-thousands:5 +7=1\n\nSo that gives 81416. Correct.\n\nThen 70846 +983365:\n\n47650 +689681.\n\nLet me write 686847 as 642,648 +15,447.\n\nAdding 69,680 to 92,721 first: 86,882 +91,622 = 913,302. Then add 583,673 to get 076,943. Yep, that works.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the answer is 682,430.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 861 and 965 is calculated as follows:.\n\nFirst, break down the multiplication using the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n861 \\times 965 = 861 \\times (900 + 60 + 5).\n\\].\n\\[.\n= (861 \\times 900) + (861 \\times 60) + (861 \\times 5).\n\\].\n\nCalculate each term separately:.\n1. \\(861 \\times 900 = 774,\\!900\\).\n2. \\(861 \\times 60 = 51,\\!660\\).\n3. \\(861 \\times 5 = 4,\\!305\\).\n\nAdd the results together:.\n\\[.\n774,\\!900 + 51,\\!660 = 826,\\!560.\n\\].\n\\[.\n826,\\!560 + 4,\\!305 = 830,\\!865.\n\\].\n\n**Final Answer:**. Therefore, the answer is"]] 88%|########7 | 438/500 [1:56:19<01:45,  1.70s/it]
