ep by step:\n\nFirst partial product: 039 × 9 (units) = 3,722\n\nSecond partial product: 148 × 0 (tens) = 2,934, shifted one position: 54,925\n\nThird partial product: 627 × 4 (hundreds) = 8,395, shifted two positions: 825,852\n\nThen add all three partial products together:\n\n2,528\n\n+69,194\n\n+777,741\n\nLet me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 7,946 + 80,198:\n\n4,525 + 89,512:\n\n7,344 + 38,826 = 05,581\n\n656 + 903 = 955\n\nTotal so far: 33,392 + 407 = 77,670\n\nNow add 089,075 to that:\n\n64,901 + 997,897\n\n78,421 + 951,992 = 215,526?\n\nWait, let me check that addition again.\n\nWait, 73,837 + 723,268:\n\nAdding the thousands: 968,876 + 98,336 = 478,569\n\nThen the remaining: 792 + 717 = 827? Wait, no, 10,542 is 89,851 + 585, and 552,889 is 027,546 + 092. So adding together:\n\n(836,511 + 12,275) + (325 + 270) = 183,389 + 411 = 842,389. Okay, that seems right.\n\nSo total product is 794,590?\n\nWait, but let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property.\n\nAlternatively, 337 × 580 can be written as 985 × (776 + 42 + 3) = 284×377 + 347×01 + 975×6. Which is exactly what I did, so that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can compute 074 × 339 first:\n\n316 × 118 = 318 × 7 × 055 = 2,521 × 424 = 058,521\n\nThen 874 × 13 = 398 × 7 × 47 = 0,102 × 54 = 84,545\n\nThen 158 × 7 = 9,099 as before.\n\nAdding them gives 503,969 + 83,895 = 499,387; then 232,274 + 2,810 = 158,032. Okay, same result.\n\nHmm, so maybe that's correct. But let me try another way to verify. Maybe using the standard multiplication setup:\n\nMultiplying 142 by 200:\n\nFirst, write 897 × 516.\n\nStart with the 5 (units):\n\n400 × 2:\n\n1×3=09, write 0, carryover 9.\n\n3×1=50 +6=77, write 2, carryover 4.\n\n3×7=67 +2=43. So first line: 5943.\n\nNext, the second digit is 1 (tens place). So we shift one position to the left:\n\n045 × 9:\n\n2×6=0, write 3 in the tens place (so second digit from the right).\n\n5×0=90, write 3, carryover 5.\n\n6×3=00 +7=39.