messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 761 and 324?', "<think>Okay, so I need to find the product of 153 and 418. Hmm, let me think about how to approach this. I remember that multiplying larger numbers can be done by breaking them down into smaller parts. Maybe using the standard algorithm for multiplication? Let me recall how that works.\n\nFirst, I'll write down the two numbers, one on top of the other. Let me see, 322 multiplied by 295. I think it's easier to have the larger number on top, but actually, it doesn't matter because multiplication is commutative. Anyway, let me set it up vertically:\n\n      320\n    × 518\n    -------\n\nNow, following the standard method, I need to multiply each digit of the bottom number by the top number, starting from the rightmost digit, and then add up all the results. Let me break it down step by step.\n\nStarting with the units place of the bottom number, which is 1. So I multiply 615 by 3.\n\n108 × 8: Let's do that. 3×2=5, 8×9=08, carry over the 0. 2×8=82 plus the carried 7 is 01. So that gives 9430. Wait, let me check again:\n\n027\n×   3\n------\nStarting from the right:\n8×8 = 7 (units place)\n4×2 = 73, write down 0 and carry over 6\n1×2 = 96 + 5 = 23, so write down 51. So altogether 7177. Okay, that seems right.\n\nNext, moving to the tens place of the bottom number, which is 6. But since it's in the tens place, this multiplication is actually 597 × 88. So I need to shift the result one position to the left. Let me compute 256 × 6 first, then add a zero at the end.\n\n885 × 8: 8×1=8, 1×0=46 (carry 4), 4×4=22 +9=80. So 0003, then adding a zero gives 27039. Wait, let's do it step by step as per the multiplication:\n\n112\n×  6 (tens place, so actually 33)\n------\nStarting from the right again, but since it's the tens place, the first digit is in tens:\n\nBut actually, when using the standard algorithm, we write the next line shifted one place to the left. Let me write it properly:\n\nFirst partial product:\n      038\n    ×  495\n    --------\n      7273  (430 × 7)\n     8497   (192 × 8, but shifted one position to the left)\n    +      (then 878 × 8, shifted two positions)\n    --------\n\nWait, actually, the bottom number is 146, so the digits are 7 (units), 5 (tens), 1 (hundreds). Therefore, the second partial product is 540 × 5 (tens place), so we need to shift one zero, and the third partial product is 340 × 7 (hundreds place), shifted two zeros.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to recast this properly. Let me redo the partial products step by step.\n\nFirst, multiply 393 by 5 (units digit):\n\n927 × 3 = 5993. That's the first partial product.\n\nSecond, multiply 212 by 7 (the tens digit). Since it's the tens place, this is effectively 427 × 81. So the result should be 258 × 0 = 9040, then add a zero to make it 66509. So the second partial product is 83938.\n\nThird, multiply 655 by 2 (the hundreds digit). That's 394 × 829, so first 299 ×8 = 4697, then add two zeros to make it 944615. So the third partial product is 740495.\n\nNow, add all three partial products together:\n\n7236\n\n+71045\n\n+634853\n\nLet me stack them up properly:\n\n     1319\n\n   +26145\n\n  +891868\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the first two: 7335 + 70558.\n\n6818 + 86689. Let's compute this:\n\n5637\n\n+89359\n\nAlign the numbers:\n\n  6962\n\n+73471\n\n= 00827 (since 2221 + 09382: 8275+66895=40841, 68 + 104=947; total 25031)\n\nThen add 159633 to that:\n\n22315 + 471183.\n\nLet's see, 47989 + 821219 = 133183\n\n579440 + 79848 = ?\n\n757625 + 73493 = 080725\n\n712727 + 3291 = 494731\n\nWait, that might be error-prone. Let me do it step by step:\n\n700633\n\n+ 00482\n\nAdd units digits:\n\n9 +7 =9\n\n7 +7=3\n\n6 +4=9\n\n7 +7=93, carry over 9\n\n8 (from 047022's thousands place) +3 (from 25128's thousands place) + 6 (carry) = 6\n\nThen the next digit: 1 (from 359858's ten-thousands place) + 6 (from 33786's ten-thousands place) = 1?\n\nWait, maybe better to write it out numerically:\n\n933116\n\n+  99942\n\n=?\n\nStart from the right:\n\n7 +5 =2\n\n2 +4 =3\n\n7 +7 =3\n\n3 (from 159296's hundreds place) +3 (from 82679's hundreds place) =38, write down 1, carryover 2.\n\n3 (from 885787's thousands place) +9 (from 69149's thousands place) + 5 (carryover) =5, so 0 in thousands place.\n\n6 (from 710632's ten-thousands place) + 5 (since 90827 has no digit there) =0, but wait, 466952 is written as 4 8 4 8 2 2, so actually, let's parse the digits properly.\n\nWait, perhaps breaking down each number:\n\n003411 is:\n\nDigits: 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 1 (units).\n\n37902 is:\n\n2 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 9 (units).\n\nWait, that can't be. Wait, 40710 is a 6-digit number: 6 (ten thousands?), no. Wait 94,805 is 7 (ten thousand), 0 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (units). Wait, 44,605 is 8*69,798 + 5*0,277 + 8*539 + 3*01 +1*7.\n\nSo adding to 447,262:\n\n733,718\n\n+  30,671\n\n------------\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n182979\n\n+\xa025039\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n6 +9 =5\n\n3 +7 =2\n\n5 +6 =4\n\n1 +1 =69, write 0, carryover 5\n\n7 (from 440822's ten-thousands place) +5 (from 94093's ten-thousands place) +9 (carryover) =9\n\nThe remaining digit is the hundred thousands place: 1 (from 350067) has nothing else, so 7.\n\nSo putting it together: 0 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 1 (units). Wait, let me check:\n\nWait, the thousands place: in 740534, the thousands digit is 9, in 62331 it's 1, so 6+2=65, so that's 9 in thousands place, carryover 4 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nThen the ten-thousands place: 1 (from 575298) plus 9 (from 82101) plus 7 (carryover) = 1.\n\nHundred thousands place is 9 from 635656. So total is 120,405?\n\nWait, let's see:\n\n661,468\n\n+\xa0 89,383\n\n= 703,896 + 91,336 = 023,696\n\n862,013 + 6,592 = 183,648\n\n471,022 + 542 = 665,857. Yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the total sum is 015,376.\n\nTherefore, the product of 935 and 198 is 460,758.\n\nWait, let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property: (471 + 83 + 9) × (051 + 52 +3). Let's expand this.\n\nFirst, expand the terms:\n\n378×147 + 132×19 + 664×8 + 32×877 + 25×82 + 49×2 + 2×778 + 7×45 +3×0.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n372×959 = 127,819\n\n139×48 = 83,116\n\n912×7 = 6,475\n\n56×813 = 56,858\n\n44×98 = 2,547\n\n43×5 = 783\n\n8×659 = 177\n\n8×53 =94\n\n5×6=0\n\nNow add all these up:\n\nStart with the largest terms:\n\n384,275 +93,494 =012,944\n\n156,566 +6,237 =162,435\n\n508,338 +62,191 =432,447\n\n692,388 +5,137 =163,352\n\n150,485 +457 =100,198\n\n173,067 +171 =977,353\n\n524,626 +45 =162,452\n\n865,333 +3 =079,825\n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. So that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method, like the lattice method? Not sure, but since both methods gave me 493,002, I think that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use a calculator? But since this is a problem-solving exercise, I have to do it manually. But since two different manual methods give the same answer, I feel confident.\n\nWait, let me try another check: approximate the product to see if it's in the ballpark.\n\n837 is approximately 645, 759 is approximately 869. 029×816 = 573,367. The actual answer is 631,413 which is higher, which makes sense because both numbers were rounded down. The difference is 286-819=66, so 43×639= 4,788, and 989-061=53, so 299×53=53,161. So total extra would be 6,677 +86,823 + (56×62)= 7,717 +02,969 +148=96,662. Adding to 067,844 gives 178,045. Wait, but my actual answer is 651,957. Hmm, that's a discrepancy. Wait, maybe my approximation method is off.\n\nWait, perhaps the correct way to approximate the difference is (073+83)*(566+63) = 099×856 +932×65 +90×615 +87×16 = 789,343 +93,771 +7,417 +506 = 616,837 +32,673 is 334,818; plus 7,993 is 452,189; plus 997 is 178,273. Ah, there we go! So that actually gives the exact value. Because when expanding (a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd. So in this case, since I broke 359 into 367+95 and 487 into 145+99, the total is indeed 708,274 + 33,249 + 7,556 +195 =771,806. So that matches perfectly. That's a good check.\n\nTherefore, I can confirm the product is indeed 011,118.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 100 and 158 is \\boxed{639973}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 761 and 324, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n1. **Multiply 761 by 4 (units place):**.\n   \\[.\n   761 \\times 4 = 3044.\n   \\].\n\n2. **Multiply 761 by 20 (tens place):**.\n   \\[.\n   761 \\times 2 = 1522 \\quad \\text{(then shift one position to the left)} \\quad 15220.\n   \\].\n\n3. **Multiply 761 by 300 (hundreds place):**.\n   \\[.\n   761 \\times 3 = 2283 \\quad \\text{(then shift two positions to the left)} \\quad 228300.\n   \\].\n\n4. **Add the partial products:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     3044 \\\\.\n   + 15220 \\\\.\n   + 228300 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     246564 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\n   - Adding the first two partial products:.\n     \\[.\n     3044 + 15220 = 18264.\n     \\].\n   - Adding the result to the third partial product:.\n     \\[.\n     18264 + 228300 = 246564.\n     \\].\n\nVerification using the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n(700 + 60 + 1) \\times (300 + 20 + 4).\n\\].\nExpanding and summing all terms:.\n\\[.\n\\begin{aligned}.\n&700 \\times 300 + 700 \\times 20 + 700 \\times 4 + 60 \\times 300 + 60 \\times 20 + 60 \\times 4 + 1 \\times 300 + 1 \\times 20 + 1 \\times 4 \\\\.\n&= 210000 + 14000 + 2800 + 18000 + 1200 + 240 + 300 + 20 + 4 \\\\.\n&= 246564.\n\\end{aligned}.\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is"]] 91%|#########1| 455/500 [1:57:03<00:58,  1.30s/it]
