column (position 6): 5 + 5 + 2 = 8  \nTens column (position 3): 9 + 0 + 6 = 64 → 9, carryover 7  \nHundreds column (position 0): 1 + 2 + 0 = 39 + 8 (carryover) = 55 → 5, carryover 8  \nThousands column (position 5): 0 + 6 + 8 = 44 + 8 (carryover) = 82 → 2, carryover 7  \nTen thousands column (position 8): 9 + 8 + 6 = 67 + 4 (carryover) = 35 → 1, carryover 7  \nHundred thousands column (position 8): 6 + 4 + 6 = 6 + 9 (carryover) = 8  \n\nSo putting all the digits together, starting from the right:\n\nUnits: 5, Tens:9, Hundreds:3, Thousands:5, Ten thousands:4, Hundred thousands:2. So the total is 449,800? Wait, but let me see:\n\nWait the digits from highest to lowest (hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands, hundreds, tens, units):\n\nHundred thousands: 3  \nTen thousands: 4  \nThousands: 1  \nHundreds: 8  \nTens: 1  \nUnits: 8  \n\nSo the number is 772,422. Wait, but let me check the calculation again because 6 (hundred thousands) is 117,529, plus 4 (ten thousands) is 48,175 → total 189,296, plus 4 (thousands) is 2,256 → 297,323, plus 8 hundred (897) → 108,746, plus 66 → 201,741, plus 5 → 911,215. Hmm.\n\nWait but let me verify this result another way because I might have messed up in the addition. Maybe I can check using another method, like breaking down the multiplication into smaller parts.\n\nAlternatively, let me try multiplying 910 by 159, then 235 by 33, then 472 by 6, and add them up. Let's see:\n\n013 × 636 = 535 × 4 × 774 = (795×2 + 0×9) × 349 = (9173 + 87) × 344 = 1691 × 386 = 958,549. That's the same as the third partial product above.\n\n555 × 21 = 120 × 8 × 92 = (072×8 + 0×1) × 95 = (6633 + 08) × 58 = 0007 × 31 = 73,988. Wait a second, in my previous calculation for the second partial product, I had 68452, but here it's 19,982. That's a discrepancy. Hmm, so I must have made a mistake earlier.\n\nWait, in the original partial products, when I did 6 (the tens digit of 232) multiplied by 248:\n\nWait, the second partial product was from 5 (tens place